INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('continued-growth-surge-anticipated-in-the-european-point-of-sale-software-market-by-2030', 'Continued Growth Surge Anticipated in the European Point of Sale Software Market by 2030', 'Future Trends and Key Innovations in the Europe Point-of-Sale Software Market', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Future Trends and Key Innovations in the Europe Point-of-Sale Software Market"},{"type":"p","text":"According to Precision Business Insights, in its latest release, the firm notes that the Europe Point-of-Sale Software Market was valued at USD 5,700 million in 2023 and is expected to witness a CAGR of 9.84% during the forecast period, 2024 to 2030. The increasing key factors expected to drive demand in the point-of-sale software market are personalized shopping experience and effective dynamic pricing optimization. This would be a key innovation that would characterize the business environment, the very incorporation of generative AI. Generative AI will make it possible to offer very personalized shopping experiences based on data about clients: Kob Kronik, personalized recommendations, targeted rewards, and customized point-of-sale interfaces."},{"type":"p","text":"This innovation in the process would not only add to consumer satisfaction and loyalty but also enhance the implementation of dynamic pricing plans in real-time, hence increasing the profitability of the firms. More interestingly, generative AI boosts point-of-sale Software''s fraud detection capabilities by analyzing transaction patterns and detecting the deviations of the same in real-time, thereby improving the overall security of transactions. The introduction of these advanced technologies brings innovation and efficiency into the Point-of-Sale sector, helping businesses deliver more enhanced and frictionless experiences to consumers as well as retailers by integrating these technologies."},{"type":"p","text":"Handheld Point of Sale is the Game Changer for the Point-of-sale Software Market:"},{"type":"p","text":"By Device type, the market is segmented into Mobile point of sale, Tablet point of sale, Desktop/ Traditional point of sale, PIN pad, and Others. On one hand, among these, Mobile Point of Sale is estimated to register a growth of 11.06% CAGR over the historical period. The segment is likely to increase by 10.53 % CAGR during the forecast period and touch US$ 562.3 Million by 2030. Since COVID-19 broke out, mobile Point of Sale systems have gained a lot of traction, gaining over 10 million mobile payments in the United Kingdom. In 2023, there will be approximately £259 billion worth of digital transactions in the UK, which will be more than a third."},{"type":"p","text":"According to PWC, by 2030, cashless transactions will have tripled, and this may point to the significance of mobile Point of Sale systems. More solutions are being done on Point of Sale technology with creativity and trend-setting. One of the key drivers in the mobile Point of Sale market is companies aiming to improve the customer experience. Mobile Point of Sale solutions help companies eliminate payment lines by allowing customers to pay for goods and services before getting to the counter, thereby greatly increasing their satisfaction and loyalty to the brand. In addition to this factor, their low price, security in transactions, and user-friendly interfaces are helping in their adoption largely by small and medium-sized businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"The Demand for the Retail Sector in the Point-of-sale Software Market:"},{"type":"p","text":"Segmentation based on Application: Restaurant, Hospitality, Healthcare, Retail, Warehouse/Distribution, Others. Among these, the Retail segment is projected to grow at a CAGR of 11.5 % during the historical period (2019 - 2023). The segment is expected to grow at a CAGR of 10.67% during the forecast period and reach US$ 567.4 Million in 2030. Increasing traditional and new retail outlets in the region of Europe acts as a driver for Point of Sale Software demand. This growth is encouraged by rapid urbanization, higher disposable incomes, and changing consumer lifestyles. Retail has seen an element of digital transformation itself, with the advent of not only omnichannel retailing, mobile, and contactless payments but also other solutions including cloud-based point-of-sale systems."},{"type":"p","text":"E-marketer statistics reveal that besides the interest in this powerful Point-of-sale feature, most retailers need modern point-of-sale solutions to match the processing of many payment methods, deliver real-time data, and offer a unified shopping experience across online and physical storefronts. The data-driven Point of Sale Software offers total insights into the inventory trends, consumer behavior, and sales patterns that enhance operational efficiency and ensure much more personalized consumer experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"Russia Leads the Point of Sale Market"},{"type":"p","text":"Leading the Point-of-sale Software Market, Russia is expected to grow at a CAGR of 10.6% during the historical period 2019-2023. The same segment is estimated to grow at 9.82% in the forecast period and the values will reach US$ 1,845.81 million by 2030. The massive expanse of land and logistic complexities require state-of-the-art Point of Sale software systems to drive the retail sector in Russia. Such technologies are essential for the proper execution of activities with such a large population base and for handling any issues in the supply chain."},{"type":"p","text":"However, it is a formidable Point of Sale technology that, despite economic uncertainties and geopolitical conflicts, the greatest impediment to foreign investment, drives the Russian retail industry for better customer experience, inventory management, and market change. As such, it is the largest market in the EMEA Point of Sale software market. Additionally, market growth in the point of sale (POS) industry is quite significantly being fuelled by the utilization of already existing technologies such as Near Field Communication (NFC) and biometric authentication."},{"type":"p","text":"NFC technology enables quick transactions that are contactless, as different devices communicate with each other nearby, such as a smartphone and a card. This enables fast transactions, which ease the process for any customer or business. Consequently, it is highly favored in any retail setup where speed is of the essence. Biometric authentication achieves its high security by verifying identity during, for instance, transactions, through unique biological characteristics like fingerprints, facial recognition, or iris scans."},{"type":"p","text":"This enhances not only safety but also ease of business in authentication processes that traditionally were cumbersome for its requirements such as PIN digits or signature verification. These are, therefore, technologies of the essence to drive growth in the market of Russia by updating merchants'' operations to meet the changing expectations of their core customers in a more digital and security-conscious environment."},{"type":"p","text":"Strategic Expansion, Mergers, Collaborations, and Agreements are the key Strategies Adopted by Market Players:"},{"type":"p","text":"Market players in the environment implement a hybrid of the strategies of the mentioned diversity to survive, increase growth, and take advantage of their respective shipments. Indeed, companies invest in capabilities that enhance the opportunity within themselves to answer increased demand in the packaging and printing industry; this implementation involves entering areas of manufacturing new products and/ or leveraging existing competence and infrastructure in the drives to diversify their activities."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/7e7af0_1dc2f448365447c5be750ca262812115~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_3000,h_2000,al_c,q_90/News%20-%20Aug%2007.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-08-07', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('luxury-redefined:-india-international-hospitality-expo-2024-showcases-top-brands', 'Luxury Redefined: India International Hospitality Expo 2024 Showcases Top Brands', 'Exclusive Insights into the Luxury Trends Shaping the Hospitality Industry', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Exclusive Insights into the Luxury Trends Shaping the Hospitality Industry"},{"type":"p","text":"The India International Hospitality Expo (IHE) 2024, scheduled from August 3rd to 6th at India Expo Centre & Mart, Greater Noida, Delhi NCR, is set to be a transformative event for the hospitality industry. With over 1000 exhibitors and an expected attendance exceeding 20,000 B2B buyers, this seventh edition is primed to be a significant occasion, featuring an extensive array of products and services from luxury hotels, resorts, restaurants, and more."},{"type":"p","text":"Core Features of IHE 2024"},{"type":"p","text":"Joint Events"},{"type":"p","text":"IHE 2024 gains additional traction by being co-located with four other major events pertinent to the hospitality sector: Catering Asia, Tent Décor Asia, and AYURYOG EXPO. This amalgamation offers a versatile solution to meet diverse industry requirements, bringing the latest trends and innovations under one roof while fostering valuable networking opportunities."},{"type":"p","text":"Global Collaborations"},{"type":"p","text":"Vietnam takes center stage as the Partner Country for this year''s expo, introducing a rich cultural facet. Esteemed Vietnamese Chefs Phem Van Dong and Nguyen Van Thong are set to conduct masterclasses alongside renowned Indian chefs Chef Nandlal and Chef Gautam. Moreover, Himachal Pradesh will be highlighted as the Focus State, promoting its tourist appeal and adding to the event’s cultural diversity."},{"type":"p","text":"Exhibitor Highlights"},{"type":"p","text":"Prominent brands such as TOPS INDIA, VENUS, ANUPAM ROYALS, BOON, and others will showcase their latest offerings. As a Golden Partner, TOPS INDIA will display its extensive line of convenience and processed food products. The vast participation of over 1000 exhibitors across four intertwined shows will encompass a wide range of industry sectors."},{"type":"p","text":"Support from Industry Associations"},{"type":"p","text":"Esteemed Associations"},{"type":"p","text":"IHE 2024 enjoys the support of distinguished industry organizations like HOTREMAI, ARCHII, Nippon Global, IIID Delhi Chapter, PPF, and HRANI. With HRANI organizing its Annual Conclave during the expo, and IIID acting as a knowledge partner, the event will offer invaluable sector-specific insights and opportunities."},{"type":"p","text":"Engaging Culinary Events"},{"type":"p","text":"The event will host the Hospitality Sourcing Gala, featuring several thrilling culinary competitions such as:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Pastry Queen India Competition","Master Bakers Challenge India 2024","India Pizza League Championship"]},{"type":"p","text":"These competitions provide a platform for young professionals and chefs to demonstrate and refine their culinary talents."},{"type":"p","text":"Broad Coverage"},{"type":"p","text":"Diverse Sectors"},{"type":"p","text":"IHE 2024 will address essential sectors including HoReCa (Hotel, Restaurant, and Catering), Operating Supplies & Equipment, Hospitality Technology, Food & Beverages, Housekeeping & Janitorial, Maintenance & Engineering, Furniture, Fixtures, Equipment, Facilities Management, and Cleaning & Hygiene."},{"type":"p","text":"An Epochal Event"},{"type":"p","text":"As an eagerly awaited B2B Expo, IHE 2024 is poised to be a pivotal platform for sourcing, innovation, and industry growth, cementing its status as a key event for the global hospitality community."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', '', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-08-05', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('from-touchscreens-to-tastebuds:-navigating-restaurant-branding-in-a-high-tech-world', 'From Touchscreens to Tastebuds: Navigating Restaurant Branding in a High-Tech World', 'The Digital Revolution in Restaurant Branding', '[{"type":"h2","text":"The Digital Revolution in Restaurant Branding"},{"type":"p","text":"In the competitive restaurant industry, a balanced blend of brand consistency and operational efficiency is the recipe for sustained success. Specifically in the case of multi-location businesses, maintaining consistent brand marketing will help to stand out amongst the crowd, resulting in brand loyalty among consumers and an array of other benefits. In today’s digital era, it’s no surprise that technology is the secret ingredient to enhancing marketing strategies for restaurants. From signage to targeted digital promotions to menu design, using technology can ensure that every marketing asset resonates with the brand’s overall message and identity."},{"type":"p","text":"Brand inconsistency can be the downfall of a business, which is why platforms that streamline marketing initiatives and processes are crucial. These platforms enable centralized management of branding assets, ensuring that all locations apply the same visuals and messaging, with so many restaurant brands having locations in different regions of the country, this is an especially helpful feature. Additionally, utilizing technology allows businesses more insight on customer trends and behaviors, which gives a leg up on competitors who aren’t receiving any feedback or analytics on their marketing and branding efforts."},{"type":"p","text":"Ultimately, leveraging technology not only benefits operational efficiency but also strengthens brand perception and customer engagement across all locations, which gives a brand a competitive edge in a crowded market."},{"type":"p","text":"Brand Asset Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Effective brand management requires consistent and cohesive visual and digital assets across all touchpoints, from in-store signage to online/social media marketing campaigns. When a business uses a technology-driven brand management platform, it gains access to a centralized hub for branded and customizable marketing assets."},{"type":"p","text":"These systems provide a secure location for logos, taglines, promotional materials, color schemes, and more, that are accessible to authorized users across the system. This means that individual locations can customize assets while adhering to set brand guidelines, thus enhancing brand visibility regardless of geographical location."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest brands strike a balance between consistency and personalization. By leveraging a technology-driven centralized hub, businesses can maintain consistency while simultaneously adapting marketing strategies to meet evolving consumer preferences and market trends. This provides a significant advantage over competitors who either ignore the wants and needs of consumers in different markets or neglect brand guidelines altogether resulting in marketing inconsistency."},{"type":"p","text":"By adopting brand management platforms as a resource, multi-location businesses can streamline the creation and implementation of marketing materials, maintain the control of assets, and enforce brand guidelines consistently across locations. When all of these marketing elements are combined into one fully integrated platform, businesses are able to save roughly 30 percent by cutting back on additional third-party tools. The approach not only provides operational improvements, but also fuels brand awareness through consistent visibility."},{"type":"p","text":"Real-Time Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"Technology is a game changer when it comes to businesses having access to real-time analytics. Not only does technology improve the management of marketing assets, but it also provides real-time data and analytics that give owners insight into the performance of marketing campaigns across locations, allowing brands to adapt campaigns and future strategies in real-time. This capability enhances decision-making and enables businesses to swiftly respond to market trends, optimize resource allocation, and ultimately improve efficiency and effectiveness in reaching target audiences."},{"type":"p","text":"The benefits of real-time analytics extend beyond marketing. Another key area that greatly benefits is the monitoring and management of funds and co-op dollars. Effective financial oversight is crucial for the sustainable growth of a business, and brand management platforms offer comprehensive metrics, insights, and customizable reporting tools. These tools help marketing teams monitor and manage funds and co-op dollars, oversee spending at a national and local level, and increase visibility into campaign costs. This synergy between marketing and financial operations allows for insight into the effectiveness of campaigns and the impact of each dollar invested."},{"type":"p","text":"All-in-all, being able to access real-time analytics enhances transparency and accountability within organizations. It allows teams to track the return on investment (ROI) of marketing campaigns more accurately, ensuring funds are allocated properly to maximize profitability. This integration streamlines operations and strengthens the financial health of a business."},{"type":"p","text":"Production Support for Multi-Location Businesses"},{"type":"p","text":"Brand management platforms, often developed by or in partnership with printing and marketing service brands, play a crucial role in enabling multi-location businesses to efficiently produce and distribute marketing assets. These platforms streamline the process by allowing businesses to place direct orders, which are then managed through integrated systems that facilitate the development and printing of physical branding items such as menus, pamphlets, in-store signage, and employee apparel, among others."},{"type":"p","text":"A key advantage of these brand management platforms is the ability to leverage nearby printing locations for convenient fulfillment. This localized approach not only ensures quicker turnaround times but also contributes to significant cost-savings for businesses by reducing shipping distances and associated costs. Additionally, optimizing the use of nearby resources means that businesses can minimize their carbon footprint, aligning with broader sustainability goals."},{"type":"p","text":"Overall, brand management platforms are pivotal in enhancing operational efficiency for multi-location businesses, offering a seamless solution for producing and distributing essential marketing materials while also promoting sustainability through localized production and streamlined supply chain operations."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_a5d82a899a7e40c0aec2ddcb4860f768~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%202%20(1).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-08-01', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('restaurant-weeks:-a-culinary-journey-through-time-honored-classics', 'Restaurant Weeks: A Culinary Journey Through Time-Honored Classics', 'The Essence of Tradition: Why Classics Remain Restaurant Week Favorites', '[{"type":"h2","text":"The Essence of Tradition: Why Classics Remain Restaurant Week Favorites"},{"type":"p","text":"This week, the foodservice world was treated to a robust discussion featuring a senior menu editor from a prominent food industry publication and a senior food & beverage editor from a leading restaurant news outlet. The conversation focused on national food holidays, events that elicit a mixed bag of opinions but are undeniable marketing assets in today''s challenging economic landscape."},{"type":"p","text":"The Mixed Blessing of Food Holidays"},{"type":"p","text":"Both editors expressed their hesitancy toward the genuine appeal of national food holidays. However, they were quick to acknowledge the promotional value these events bring to the table. \"Despite the skepticism, well-planned promotions around these holidays can be effective marketing tools and vital traffic drivers, particularly as costs rise and guest counts decline,\" noted one editor."},{"type":"p","text":"A Classic Mexican Restaurant: A Test of Time"},{"type":"p","text":"During her exploration of timeless eateries, the senior menu editor recounted her recent visit to a classic Mexican restaurant in New York City''s East Village that has weathered the test of time for over two decades. Praising the Margaritas and churros exceptionally, she also noted her overall satisfaction with the experience. \"It was a relief and joy to see the restaurant bustling,\" she shared, underscoring the importance of reliable, longstanding operators in the industry."},{"type":"p","text":"Brooklyn’s Culinary Landmark"},{"type":"p","text":"The senior food & beverage editor has been delving into his new neighborhood of Sheepshead Bay in Brooklyn, N.Y., and highlighted a bar and restaurant with a decades-long heritage. Much like the Mexican restaurant, this bar offers a menu packed with generous portions of solid and satisfying fare. His experience reinforced the idea that established businesses with a legacy can still hold strong appeal in ever-changing urban landscapes."},{"type":"p","text":"Maximizing Restaurant Week: Quality Over Quantity"},{"type":"p","text":"The duo moved on to discuss a city’s Restaurant Week, which defies its name with an expansion to a month-long festival this year. They touched upon strategies to make the most out of the event, emphasizing the importance of quality. \"Don''t skimp; put your best foot forward,\" they advised. This highlighted a crucial approach: leveraging top-tier offerings to attract and retain discerning customers."},{"type":"p","text":"A Seafood Restaurant''s Innovative Beverage Program"},{"type":"p","text":"The discussion also veered to the innovative beverage scene, featuring clips from an interview with a beverage director at a seafood-focused restaurant in San Francisco. The director oversees an ambitious beverage program, notably including house-distilled gin featuring seaweed as its primary botanical. This hints at the potential for restaurants to carve unique niches by pushing the boundaries of traditional offerings."},{"type":"p","text":"Non-Alcoholic Beverage Pairings"},{"type":"p","text":"In addition, the beverage director elaborated on the non-alcoholic beverage pairings available at the restaurant. These, too, are crafted in-house, offering an alternative that does not sacrifice the experience. \"Each non-alcoholic pairing is carefully, thoughtfully created,\" he detailed, providing insight into the meticulous process behind these offerings."},{"type":"p","text":"Emerging Trends: Hop Water, Matcha, and Prix-Fixe Menus"},{"type":"p","text":"In related news, the industry is noticing an upward trend in hop water, matcha, and thoughtfully crafted prix-fixe menus. These elements are reshaping consumer expectations and driving a renewed interest in flavorful, health-conscious dining experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"The conversation highlighted that while food holidays may not be universally beloved, they offer a stage for classic eateries and innovative beverage programs to shine, proving the enduring appeal and evolving dynamism of the restaurant industry."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_4a90d22e400a44cf966acade730c5295~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%202.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-30', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('digital-temptations:-how-online-food-ordering-boosts-indulgence-and-spending-habits', 'Digital Temptations: How Online Food Ordering Boosts Indulgence and Spending Habits', 'Unveiling the Research on Digital Food Ordering Habits', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Unveiling the Research on Digital Food Ordering Habits"},{"type":"p","text":"As restaurants increasingly embrace technology for placing food orders, a new University of South Florida study reveals that digital ordering platforms significantly influence consumer behavior, often leading to more indulgent food choices and increased spending."},{"type":"p","text":"Study Overview and Key Findings"},{"type":"p","text":"Co-authored by Dipayan Biswas, the USF Frank Harvey endowed professor of marketing in the Muma College of Business, the comprehensive study compares the cognitive effects of ordering from a digital screen to traditional methods, including printed menus."},{"type":"p","text":"The research, published in the Journal of the Academy of Marketing Science, highlights the shift towards digital ordering in major food chains introducing touchscreen kiosks and tabletop tablets. The growth of app-based delivery services such as Uber Eats, Grubhub, and DoorDash since the COVID-19 pandemic further illustrates this trend."},{"type":"p","text":"Pandemic-Induced Changes in Food Acquisition"},{"type":"p","text":"According to the U.S. Department of Agriculture Economic Research Service, the pandemic significantly altered how U.S. consumers acquire food, particularly through carryout and delivery services. Spending on third-party delivery tripled for quick-service restaurants and nearly quadrupled for full-service restaurants from pre-pandemic levels to late 2022."},{"type":"p","text":"\"While digital ordering can enhance convenience and efficiency, many consumers will opt for unhealthier food choices and spend more,\" Biswas said. \"Our research highlights the importance of understanding the influence of digital devices on our decision-making.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Detailed Research Methodology"},{"type":"p","text":"Through six studies at various restaurants and two in a USF School of Marketing and Innovation lab, Biswas and his graduate students examined the effects of ordering from a digital menu versus a physical menu. The team reviewed more than 23,000 orders from diverse dining establishments, including an independently owned Mexican cuisine restaurant and a global dining chain with 1,000 locations across 23 countries."},{"type":"p","text":"Notable Findings and Food Categorization"},{"type":"p","text":"The study revealed that 61% of digital orders, including those made for delivery, were unhealthy, more than 3% higher than non-digital orders. Each item was categorized as unhealthy, neutral, or healthy. Unhealthy items consisted of large portions and choices like fried foods and desserts, while items like vegetables and fish were considered healthy. Most soups, large salads, and steaks smaller than six ounces were deemed neutral."},{"type":"p","text":"The research also found that digital menus have a greater impact on dinner orders, as consumers tend to be more exhausted and reliant on technology later in the day. Therefore, digital ordering technologies may influence breakfast and lunch choices to a lesser extent."},{"type":"p","text":"\"Digital ordering modes foster a more automatic decision-making process with lower cognitive involvement,” Biswas noted. “This is because digital tools encourage people to rely less on their cognitive resources and more on automated processes.”"},{"type":"p","text":"The “Google Effect” and Consumer Proficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"This phenomenon, known as the \"Google Effect,\" suggests that the availability of digital tools alters how people store and retrieve information. This reduced cognitive involvement in digital contexts can lead to more automatic decision-making, resulting in more indulgent food choices. The study revealed that consumers proficient with technology might be less affected by this phenomenon."},{"type":"p","text":"Implications for Restaurant Managers"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Restaurant managers aiming to promote healthier options may benefit from offering non-digital ordering modes, or some may be interested in promoting indulgent items during dinner hours through digital ordering to drive sales,\" said Biswas."},{"type":"p","text":"Future Research Directions"},{"type":"p","text":"Biswas plans to continue this research to further examine how the presence of a human, such as when ordering in person or on the phone, may impact consumers'' decisions. He also aims to investigate how digital versus non-digital modes affect a consumer''s consumption volume and perceived taste of ordered items."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_00658963fdba4c21aee765a4f0a9d4fb~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Industry%20news%201.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-25', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('national-candy-month:-a-golden-opportunity-for-summer-confectionery-sales', 'National Candy Month: A Golden Opportunity for Summer Confectionery Sales', 'A Sweet Celebration: Highlighting the Joy of Candy', '[{"type":"h2","text":"A Sweet Celebration: Highlighting the Joy of Candy"},{"type":"p","text":"In the heart of summer, National Candy Month provides a sweet boost to the confectionery industry. Celebrated throughout June, this month-long event highlights the joys of candy and drives significant sales, creating a golden opportunity for confectionery retailers and manufacturers to maximize their profits."},{"type":"p","text":"A Sweet Celebration"},{"type":"p","text":"National Candy Month brings attention to the wide variety of candies that delight consumers of all ages. From classic favorites to innovative new treats, this celebration provides a platform for brands to showcase their products."},{"type":"p","text":"“National Candy Month is a perfect time for us to connect with our customers and introduce new products,” said an industry executive."},{"type":"p","text":"Boosting Summer Sales"},{"type":"p","text":"Historically, National Candy Month has led to a significant increase in confectionery sales. According to the National Confectioners Association (NCA), candy sales often see a notable rise during June."},{"type":"p","text":"“We always see a spike in sales during National Candy Month,” noted a marketing director in the confectionery industry."},{"type":"p","text":"Marketing and Promotions"},{"type":"p","text":"Retailers and manufacturers capitalize on National Candy Month with special promotions, limited-edition products, and engaging marketing campaigns. These strategies not only drive sales but also build brand loyalty."},{"type":"p","text":"“Our National Candy Month campaigns are designed to be fun and engaging,” shared a vice president of marketing at a leading confectionery company."},{"type":"p","text":"Innovative Product Launches"},{"type":"p","text":"Many confectionery companies use National Candy Month as a launchpad for new products. Introducing fresh flavors and unique candy concepts during this period can generate buzz and attract new customers."},{"type":"p","text":"“Launching new products during National Candy Month gives us a great platform to reach a wider audience,” said a head of product development at a major candy brand."},{"type":"p","text":"Sampling and Events"},{"type":"p","text":"To drive engagement and consumer interest, candy brands often host sampling events and participate in community activities. These hands-on experiences allow customers to try new candies and create memorable connections with the brand."},{"type":"p","text":"“We host tasting events and sponsor local festivals to celebrate National Candy Month,” explained a brand manager at a confectionery company."},{"type":"p","text":"Consumer Trends and Insights"},{"type":"p","text":"National Candy Month provides valuable insights into consumer preferences and trends. By analyzing sales data and customer feedback, companies can better understand what works and adapt their strategies accordingly."},{"type":"p","text":"“The data we gather during National Candy Month helps shape our future product development,” stated a senior analyst at a confectionery corporation."},{"type":"p","text":"Community and Charity Initiatives"},{"type":"p","text":"Many companies use National Candy Month as an opportunity to give back to the community. By partnering with local charities and organizing fundraising events, candy brands can enhance their corporate social responsibility efforts."},{"type":"p","text":"“We believe in giving back, especially during National Candy Month,” said a community outreach coordinator at a confectionery company."},{"type":"p","text":"Looking Ahead"},{"type":"p","text":"As National Candy Month continues to grow in popularity, the confectionery industry can look forward to even greater opportunities for engagement and sales. With innovative products, compelling marketing, and a strong community presence, brands can leverage this sweet celebration to boost their summer sales significantly."},{"type":"p","text":"“National Candy Month is a highlight of our year,” concluded an industry leader. “It’s a chance to celebrate the joy of candy and connect with our customers in meaningful ways.”"},{"type":"p","text":"For more information on National Candy Month and its impact on the confectionery industry, visit the National Confectioners Association website."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_cc4a7efd222a4dc598a4a553dc95f3e2~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/New%202.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-24', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('school-foodservice-leaders-converge-in-boston-for-anc24-conference', 'School Foodservice Leaders Converge in Boston for ANC24 Conference', 'A Hub of Innovation: Boston Hosts ANC24', '[{"type":"h2","text":"A Hub of Innovation: Boston Hosts ANC24"},{"type":"p","text":"From July 14th to July 16th, the 2024 Annual National Conference (ANC) of the School Nutrition Association (SNA) turned Boston into a bustling hub for over 6,000 school lunch service workers. This eagerly awaited event offered all-expense-paid trips for attendees, providing an unparalleled opportunity for education, networking, and sampling a wide variety of nutritious foods."},{"type":"p","text":"A Storied History"},{"type":"p","text":"Founded in 1946, the SNA is a national, non-profit professional organization representing 50,000 school nutrition professionals across the United States. The association is dedicated to ensuring healthy school meals and nutrition education for all students. The Annual National Conference is recognized as the School Nutrition Event of the Year, uniting thousands of school nutrition program operators, industry partners, and allied organizations each July."},{"type":"p","text":"Education and Exhibits Galore"},{"type":"p","text":"The three-day event featured more than 120 education sessions and over 800 exhibit booths. Attendees engaged in various networking events designed to inspire innovative approaches and dynamic ideas for reimagining school nutrition operations. The conference kicked off with a keynote speech by Chef Andrew Zimmern and concluded with insights from Astronaut Jose Hernandez."},{"type":"p","text":"Addressing Contemporary Challenges"},{"type":"p","text":"The ANC is renowned for its comprehensive exhibits and education sessions aimed at helping attendees prepare nutritious and delicious school meals while managing budget constraints, a tight labor market, strict nutrition standards, and diverse student preferences. This year''s conference was particularly significant, following the release of long-term nutrition standards that require schools to reduce sodium in meals further and adhere to new limits on added sugars."},{"type":"p","text":"Innovative Menu Options"},{"type":"p","text":"Attendees had the chance to taste-test new recipes and menu options with reduced added sugars and salts, such as a reduced-sodium, whole grain Orange Chicken Stir Fry, and reduced-sugar yogurt without artificial sweeteners, flavors, or colors. Culinary demonstrations and workshops offered tips for expanding scratch cooking, including an in-depth session on Boston Public Schools’ transition to scratch meals."},{"type":"p","text":"Culturally Relevant and Plant-Based Options"},{"type":"p","text":"The conference also showcased culturally relevant and plant-based menu options reflecting diverse student tastes, with recipes like Cilantro Lime Brown Rice with Black Beans and Southwest Sauce, and Cheesy Chicken Shawarma. Best practices for accommodating food allergies and special dietary needs, such as Kosher and Halal, were also shared."},{"type":"p","text":"Recognizing Excellence"},{"type":"p","text":"The SNA recognized school nutrition professionals who go above and beyond with national and state awards. The ANC was not only an educational event but also a celebration of the dedication and hard work of those who ensure students receive nutritious meals every day."},{"type":"p","text":"Ongoing Support and Resources"},{"type":"p","text":"In addition to the conference, the SNA offers ongoing resources for its members, including the School Nutrition magazine and the podcast \"School Food for Thought,\" keeping school nutrition professionals informed and inspired year-round."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_f95ad367f254470ba4b733613690578b~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/New%201.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-23', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('the-burnout-buster:-the-crucial-role-of-restaurant-managers-in-employee-well-being', 'The Burnout Buster: The Crucial Role of Restaurant Managers in Employee Well-being', 'Beyond the Kitchen: Restaurant Managers as Employee Well-being Champions', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Beyond the Kitchen: Restaurant Managers as Employee Well-being Champions"},{"type":"p","text":"Across America, the restaurant industry is facing a silent crisis: burnout. The high-pressure environment, long hours, and demanding customers are taking a toll on employees, impacting morale, productivity, and ultimately, the bottom line. But amidst this challenge, a beacon of hope emerges: the restaurant manager."},{"type":"p","text":"The Burnout Antidote: Effective Management"},{"type":"p","text":"More than just taskmasters, effective managers hold the power to transform the workplace into a thriving environment where employees feel valued, motivated, and resilient to burnout. This transformation hinges on key principles:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Empowering Through Recognition: Acknowledgement is a potent motivator. Celebrate individual and team achievements, both big and small, to foster a sense of pride and purpose.","Transparent Communication: Open and honest communication is the bedrock of trust. Encourage feedback, address concerns promptly, and keep employees informed to create a collaborative atmosphere.","Leading with Integrity: Honesty and ethical behavior are non-negotiable. Managers must model the standards they expect from their team, creating a culture of mutual respect.","Unwavering Positivity: A positive attitude is contagious. Even amidst challenges, managers who maintain optimism and a strong work ethic inspire their team to do the same."]},{"type":"p","text":"Beyond the Menu: The Manager''s Expanding Role"},{"type":"p","text":"The modern restaurant manager is a multi-faceted professional, juggling a diverse range of responsibilities:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Financial Acumen: Understanding the financial landscape of the restaurant is crucial. Effective managers can analyze P&L statements, identify cost-saving opportunities, and make data-driven decisions that benefit both the business and its employees.","Operational Efficiency: Streamlining processes, from inventory management to staff scheduling, ensures smooth operations and minimizes unnecessary stress on the team.","HR Expertise: A working knowledge of labor laws and regulations safeguards employees'' rights and fosters a fair and inclusive workplace.","Mentorship and Growth: Investing in employee training and development not only enhances skills but also cultivates a culture of continuous improvement and career advancement."]},{"type":"p","text":"The Leadership Ripple Effect"},{"type":"p","text":"Leadership isn''t just about what gets done; it''s about how it gets done. When managers lead with empathy, integrity, and unwavering positivity, they create a ripple effect that influences the entire team. Employees feel supported, empowered, and less likely to succumb to the pressures of the job."},{"type":"p","text":"A Veteran''s Voice"},{"type":"p","text":"Bryan Dean Engledow, a seasoned restaurateur, encapsulates this leadership philosophy in his words: \"Power is not the ability to make people work, power is how the staff feels about you when the job is done.\" This highlights the importance of building genuine connections with employees, fostering loyalty, and inspiring them to give their best."},{"type":"p","text":"The Path Forward: A Call to Action"},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant industry stands at a crossroads. By prioritizing the development of effective managers, restaurants can turn the tide on burnout, create a thriving workplace, and reap the rewards of a motivated and engaged workforce. The future of the industry depends on it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_d8ce1d52abe54084bb84c0c69b6cd5f4~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Industry%20news.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-22', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('how-chicago''s-wage-hike-impacts-restaurants,-consumers,-and-the-local-economy', 'How Chicago''s Wage Hike Impacts Restaurants, Consumers, and the Local Economy', 'Chicago''s tipped minimum wage increased on July 1, 2024, marking a significant shift in the city''s labor landscape. This move, part of a five-year plan to achieve parity with the city''s standard minimum wage, has sparked', '[{"type":"h2","text":"A Rising Tide? Assessing the Impact of Chicago''s Wage Increase on Workers, Businesses, and Consumers"},{"type":"p","text":"Chicago''s tipped minimum wage increased on July 1, 2024, marking a significant shift in the city''s labor landscape. This move, part of a five-year plan to achieve parity with the city''s standard minimum wage, has sparked both celebration and concern within the restaurant industry."},{"type":"p","text":"A New Era for Tipped Workers"},{"type":"p","text":"The tipped minimum wage in Chicago rose from $9.48 per hour to $11.02, a substantial increase aimed at improving the livelihoods of servers, bartenders, and other tipped workers. This is the first step in a gradual climb toward the city''s standard minimum wage of $16.20, a move championed by labor advocates who argue that tipped workers deserve fair compensation and protection from wage instability."},{"type":"p","text":"Industry Concerns and Pushback"},{"type":"p","text":"The increase has not been without controversy. Restaurant associations have voiced concerns about the financial burden on businesses, particularly those still recovering from the pandemic''s economic impact. They fear that higher labor costs could lead to menu price increases, potentially deterring customers and reducing tips for workers."},{"type":"p","text":"Sam Toia, president of the Illinois Restaurant Association, argues that the focus should be on enforcing existing labor laws and penalizing employers who fail to pay the legally guaranteed minimum wage, rather than mandating further increases."},{"type":"p","text":"The National Landscape: A Growing Trend"},{"type":"p","text":"Chicago''s move aligns with a broader national trend toward raising the minimum wage for tipped workers. Seven states have already eliminated the tipped minimum wage, requiring all workers to be paid the full minimum wage plus tips. While legislation to raise the tipped minimum wage was proposed in 17 states this year, none passed, highlighting the ongoing debate surrounding this issue."},{"type":"p","text":"Impact on Restaurants and Consumers"},{"type":"p","text":"The potential impact of the wage increase on restaurants and consumers is a subject of intense scrutiny. Some restaurant owners fear that they will be forced to raise menu prices to offset increased labor costs, potentially leading to a decrease in customer traffic and tips. Others argue that the higher wages will attract and retain better staff, ultimately improving service and customer experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Worker Perspectives: A Mixed Bag"},{"type":"p","text":"The views of tipped workers themselves are also divided. While some welcome the increase as a much-needed boost to their income, others worry that it may backfire, leading to fewer hours or job cuts."},{"type":"p","text":"The Washington D.C. Example"},{"type":"p","text":"The experience of Washington, D.C., which implemented a similar law last year, offers a cautionary tale. While the number of employees at limited-service restaurants increased, full-service restaurants saw a decline in employment. Whether this trend is directly attributable to the wage increase remains unclear, but it underscores the complex and unpredictable nature of the issue."},{"type":"p","text":"A Wait-and-See Approach"},{"type":"p","text":"As Chicago''s restaurant industry adapts to the new wage landscape, the impact on businesses, workers, and consumers will be closely monitored. The success or failure of this policy could influence future decisions regarding tipped minimum wages in Chicago and beyond."},{"type":"p","text":"Looking Ahead"},{"type":"p","text":"The debate over tipped minimum wage is far from settled. As the cost of living continues to rise, the question of fair compensation for tipped workers will remain a pressing concern. It remains to be seen whether Chicago''s bold move will set a precedent for other cities and states, or whether concerns about the impact on businesses will lead to a different approach."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_22ed4722f7fd4ab188b54b1ce538937f~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%202.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-19', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('restaurant-sales-maintain-upward-trajectory-for-third-consecutive-month', 'Restaurant Sales Maintain Upward Trajectory for Third Consecutive Month', 'Dining Out on the Rise: Restaurant Sales Soar for Another Month', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Dining Out on the Rise: Restaurant Sales Soar for Another Month"},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant industry continues to show signs of steady recovery, with sales rising for the third straight month in June. This positive trend suggests a growing consumer confidence in dining out and a potential rebound for the sector."},{"type":"p","text":"June Sales Figures and Revised Data"},{"type":"p","text":"According to preliminary data from the U.S. Census Bureau, eating and drinking establishments recorded total sales of $94.8 billion on a seasonally adjusted basis in June. This figure represents a 0.3% increase from May and marks the third consecutive month of sales growth. Importantly, May''s preliminary data was revised significantly higher, painting a much more optimistic picture of the industry''s performance in the first half of 2024."},{"type":"p","text":"Resilient Labor Market and Consumer Spending"},{"type":"p","text":"The continued resilience of the labor market, coupled with the positive sales trend, suggests that consumers are likely to maintain their spending habits in the second half of the year. While economic headwinds may cause some adjustments in consumer behavior, the overall outlook remains positive for the restaurant industry."},{"type":"p","text":"Rising Menu Prices and Real Sales"},{"type":"p","text":"It''s important to note that the recent uptick in restaurant sales was primarily driven by rising menu prices. When adjusted for menu price inflation, real eating and drinking place sales remained essentially flat during the first half of 2024. In fact, June''s sales volume of $94.8 billion was $2 billion below the November 2023 peak in inflation-adjusted terms."},{"type":"p","text":"Industry Outlook and Consumer Confidence"},{"type":"p","text":"Despite the impact of inflation on real sales, the sustained growth in restaurant sales indicates a positive shift in consumer sentiment. As more people feel comfortable dining out, the industry is expected to continue its recovery trajectory. However, the ongoing challenges of inflation and supply chain disruptions will require restaurants to adapt and innovate to maintain profitability."},{"type":"p","text":"Key Takeaways"},{"type":"ul","items":["Restaurant sales rose for the third consecutive month in June, signaling a positive trend for the industry.","The resilient labor market and revised data suggest that consumer spending will likely remain stable in the second half of 2024.","Rising menu prices contributed to the sales growth, while real sales remained relatively flat.","The positive sales trend indicates growing consumer confidence in dining out, despite ongoing economic challenges."]},{"type":"p","text":"Looking Ahead"},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant industry''s ability to navigate rising costs and maintain consumer appeal will be crucial in the coming months. By focusing on innovative menu offerings, efficient operations, and enhanced customer experiences, restaurants can capitalize on the current momentum and drive further growth in the second half of 2024."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_22ed4722f7fd4ab188b54b1ce538937f~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%202.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-18', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('from-timecards-to-touchscreens:-the-digital-transformation-of-restaurant-payroll', 'From Timecards to Touchscreens: The Digital Transformation of Restaurant Payroll', 'How Technology is Transforming Restaurant Payroll: A Modern Approach', '[{"type":"h2","text":"How Technology is Transforming Restaurant Payroll: A Modern Approach"},{"type":"p","text":"The foodservice industry is undergoing significant changes, and modern payroll tools are at the forefront of this transformation. By streamlining operations, enhancing accuracy, and improving employee satisfaction, these tools are reshaping how restaurants handle payroll."},{"type":"p","text":"The Unique Challenges of Restaurant Payroll"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants face distinctive payroll challenges that differ from other industries:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Varying Shift Patterns: Flexible and often unpredictable schedules require a payroll system that can adapt effortlessly to diverse shift lengths and timing.","Tips and Additional Earnings: Accurately tracking and reporting tips adds complexity to payroll calculations, impacting both employee satisfaction and legal compliance.","Compliance with Labor Laws: The heavily regulated restaurant industry necessitates meticulous record-keeping and up-to-date knowledge of minimum wage, overtime, and break laws.","Limitations of Conventional Methods: Traditional manual data entry and paper-based systems are time-consuming, error-prone, and struggle to keep up with the dynamic nature of restaurant operations."]},{"type":"p","text":"The Rise of Modern Payroll Solutions"},{"type":"p","text":"To address these challenges, the restaurant industry is increasingly adopting modern technological solutions:"},{"type":"p","text":"Payroll Automation Tools: These tools automate tasks like wage calculation, tax withholding, and compliance with labor laws, significantly reducing the time and effort required for payroll management."},{"type":"p","text":"The Benefits of Automation in Payroll Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Automation offers a range of advantages for restaurant payroll:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Time Savings: Dramatically reduces payroll processing time, freeing up management for other responsibilities.","Increased Accuracy: Minimizes errors common in manual calculations, improving employee trust and compliance.","Compliance with Labor Laws: Tools are updated to reflect current regulations, ensuring ongoing compliance with minimal effort.","Improved Record Keeping: Digital records are easier to store, organize, and retrieve for audits and dispute resolution."]},{"type":"p","text":"Employee Satisfaction and Compliance"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern payroll technology has a significant impact on both employees and legal adherence:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Timely and Accurate Payment: Automation ensures on-time payments that accurately reflect hours worked, tips, and overtime, building trust and satisfaction.","Transparent and Accessible Pay Information: Detailed breakdowns of earnings and deductions foster fairness and transparency.","Self-Service Options: Employee portals empower staff to view paystubs, track earnings, and manage personal details.","Adherence to Labor Laws: Automated systems help restaurants comply with minimum wage, overtime, and break rules.","Tax Regulation Compliance: Tools manage tax withholdings and filings, crucial for tip reporting and other unique considerations.","Record Keeping for Audits: Detailed and organized records facilitate smooth compliance processes during audits or inspections."]},{"type":"p","text":"The Future of Restaurant Payroll Management"},{"type":"p","text":"The future holds exciting innovations:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Artificial Intelligence: AI and machine learning will bring smarter, predictive tools for labor cost insights, staffing optimization, and budgeting.","Mobile Accessibility: Payroll tasks will be handled on the go with mobile-friendly systems.","Customization and Scalability: Tools will offer tailored solutions for various restaurant types and sizes.","Data Analytics and Reporting: Enhanced reporting and analytics will provide deeper insights into payroll data for decision-making.","Employee Financial Wellness Programs: Some systems may include early wage access, savings programs, and financial education resources."]},{"type":"p","text":"In conclusion, advanced payroll technologies are not just streamlining operations but also empowering restaurants to take a strategic approach to financial management and employee engagement, driving the industry towards a more successful future."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_4cd7d0b2c8c54bbc966952d0acaa0a0c~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/142(news-blog).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-17', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('world-of-flavors-2024-to-explore-"borders,-migration,-and-the-evolution-of-culinary-tradition', 'World of Flavors 2024 to Explore "Borders, Migration, and the Evolution of Culinary Tradition', 'Beyond Borders: How Migration Transforms Our Tables (World of Flavors 2024)', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Beyond Borders: How Migration Transforms Our Tables (World of Flavors 2024)"},{"type":"p","text":"The Culinary Institute of America (CIA) has announced the theme for its highly anticipated Worlds of Flavor 2024 conference: \"Borders, Migration, and the Evolution of Culinary Tradition.\" Taking place November 6-8, 2024, at the CIA''s Copia campus in Napa Valley, the event will delve into how shifting demographics, cultural exchange, and global movements have shaped - and continue to shape - the culinary landscape."},{"type":"p","text":"A distinguished lineup of chefs, food experts, and thought leaders from around the world will share their insights on topics such as:"},{"type":"ul","items":["The impact of migration on culinary fusion and innovation: How have culinary traditions evolved as people move across borders and cultures blend?","Exploring the roots of global cuisines: What are the historical and cultural forces that have shaped the flavors and ingredients we enjoy today?","The role of food in cultural identity and storytelling: How does food preserve cultural heritage and connect us to our roots?","Culinary trends emerging from diverse communities: What new and exciting flavors are gaining popularity as a result of cultural exchange?"]},{"type":"p","text":"\"This year''s theme is particularly relevant as we witness unprecedented global migration and a growing interest in culinary diversity,\" said a CIA spokesperson. \"Worlds of Flavor 2024 will provide a platform for exploring the complex and fascinating ways that food connects us all.\""},{"type":"p","text":"The conference will feature a variety of presentations, panel discussions, cooking demonstrations, and tastings. Attendees will have the opportunity to network with industry professionals, learn about cutting-edge culinary trends, and gain a deeper understanding of the cultural significance of food."},{"type":"p","text":"Key Details:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Dates: November 6-8, 2024","Location: CIA Copia, Napa Valley, California","Registration: Opens in late summer 2024","Pricing:","Early Bird (until September 30, 2024): $1,995","Regular (after September 30, 2024): $2,295","Student Rate (limited availability): $1,495","Group Rate (5 or more): 10% discount","Website: worldsofflavor.com"]},{"type":"p","text":"Who Should Attend:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Foodservice professionals and chefs from restaurants, educational institutions, contract foodservice companies, hospitality, retail, and more.","Culinary educators","Private chefs and caterers"]},{"type":"p","text":"Additional Information:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Consultants: Special rate available, email si@culinary.edu for details.","Media: Contact Amanda Secor for media inquiries.","Cancellation Policy: Refer to the website for details."]},{"type":"p","text":"Industry professionals, food enthusiasts, and anyone interested in the intersection of food and culture are encouraged to attend. Don''t miss this opportunity to explore the rich tapestry of flavors that make up our world."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_9e9c532c4876475a9ac4eb31c080c8c8~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Blog%202.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-15', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('hungry-for-efficiency?-restaurant-management-software-market-set-for-$4.5-billion-expansion', 'Hungry for Efficiency? Restaurant Management Software Market Set for $4.5 Billion Expansion', 'AI & Digital Payments: Fueling Restaurant Management Software Growth', '[{"type":"h2","text":"AI & Digital Payments: Fueling Restaurant Management Software Growth"},{"type":"p","text":"According to a report by Technavio, the global restaurant management software market is likely to witness an increase of USD 4.50 billion from 2023 to 2027. The market is likely to rise at a compound annual growth rate of 15.85% during the forecast period. Key technological developments in artificial intelligence and the Internet of Things are significant factors driving restaurant management software."},{"type":"p","text":"Technology Advancements Driving the Market"},{"type":"p","text":"Role of AI and IoT"},{"type":"p","text":"Artificial intelligence makes possible predictive analytics in inventory management and understanding customer preference, therefore helping to realize operational efficiency and personalized service. The IoT devices, such as smart kitchen appliances and connected point-of-sale systems, make data collection easy and convenient to monitor in real time. This improves decision-making and cuts down on costs incurred. These technological innovations have been very critical, especially considering the fast embracing of digital payments and sophisticated management systems by this industry, despite the challenges involved in switching from the traditional ways."},{"type":"p","text":"Key Players Leveraging Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"These technologies are being used by industry leaders including Microsoft Corp., Fiserv Inc., and Block Inc. to propel market expansion. Their adoption of IoT and AI improves consumer experiences, optimizes processes, and keeps them competitive in a market that is evolving all the time."},{"type":"p","text":"Scope and Forecast of the Market"},{"type":"p","text":"Market Dynamics"},{"type":"p","text":"Technical analysis of the market dynamics is provided in full in Technavio''s most recent industry research report, \"Global Restaurant Management Software Market 2023-2027\". The market is fragmented in structure, and a wide range of firms are involved in its expansion. Therefore, it is anticipated that the market will continue to develop at a 15.85% annual rate, increasing by USD 4507.94 million by 2027. The study considered the years 2022 as the base year, 2023 to 2027 as the forecast period, and 2017 to 2021 as the historic era."},{"type":"p","text":"Regional Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"It involves market analysis, including a regional breakup wherein North America accounts for 48% of the market share. Key countries contributing to market growth include the United States, Canada, Germany, France, and the United Kingdom."},{"type":"p","text":"Digital Payments in the Foodservice Industry"},{"type":"p","text":"Go Digital in Transactions"},{"type":"p","text":"The shift to digital transactions in general, and particularly in the case of food service businesses, has taken over as a worldwide phenomenon. It is expected that, by 2030, almost 90% of all spending will be on digital payments in Canada. To remain in the competitive race, food service businesses are rapidly implementing digital payment solutions. Among many other advantages, such systems provide an increase in online orders, easiness of operation, logistic convenience, and a reduction in internal theft."},{"type":"p","text":"Role of Restaurant Management Software"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurant management software has been instrumental in facilitating cashless transactions and capturing all-important consumer data for insights and opportunities. Some of the big vendors in this marketplace include Clover by Fiserv, Microsoft, Square, and NCR Corp, all of which offer contactless payment solutions. This market is bound to grow further as digital transactions within the food service industry continue to rise."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurant Management Software Trends"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital Menu Boards, Integration"},{"type":"p","text":"Digital menu boards are increasingly in use, with the option for real-time updating of menus and promotions. Special dietary requests are easily sorted with advanced filtering and customization options. point of sale systems now come integrated with popular food delivery websites like GrubHub, PostMates, and Zomato, thus broadening your reach while bettering your online presence."},{"type":"p","text":"Current Investment in Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Touchscreen ordering solutions and mobile point-of-sale systems receive large investments from IT budgets. High penetration of smartphones and the internet leads to high disposable incomes, thus driving demand for AI-powered virtual assistants and IoT solutions. Cloud-based solutions, dominated by companies like ParTech, Inc., Jolt, and Brink POS, win out due to their flexibility and scalability."},{"type":"p","text":"Security in Focus"},{"type":"p","text":"Data security is the key, looking forward to delivering and earning the trust of customers. Companies are now trying to work on customer experience and customer retention through front-end software segments, Android and iOS-based, and cross-platform technologies."},{"type":"p","text":"Challenges in the Market"},{"type":"p","text":"Migration From Legacy Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"This becomes a problem when moving from traditional systems to high-end software solutions. For instance, a separate team to implement and support restaurants is an additional cost for the latter. Theory processes and security measures are to be framed to avoid the implementation of the system. More importantly| that software has to be congenial to the culture of your team while mapping those users to these lead management applications is not an easier task. Therefore, such challenges may slow down market growth in the forecast period."},{"type":"p","text":"Future Outlook"},{"type":"p","text":"Salt for Success: Digital Transformation"},{"type":"p","text":"Increased Internet penetration and better disposable incomes will fuel the management software market in the backdrop of high growth. Advanced technologies like AI, virtual assistants, voice-activated ordering systems, and chatbots transformed this industry in a manner that cloud-based solutions started outperforming on-premise solutions, and these technologies contributed to the adoption of key players like KFC, Pizza Hut, and Domino''s."},{"type":"p","text":"Improving Customer Satisfaction"},{"type":"p","text":"In demand in the present business scenario will be front-end software, more specifically one based on Android and iOS. Every business needs to keep cross-platform technologies to give smooth customer experiences, which will help in retaining them. Some of the features identified under this genre would include administrative and promotional elements, managing orders, processing payments, daily reconciliation, and data security features."},{"type":"p","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"The global restaurant management software market is likely to grow at a decent pace shortly, driven by the increasing demand from the Americas for technological inventions such as AI and IoT. Notwithstanding some hassle in replacing the traditional system with a new one, it is supported by changing consumer behavior towards digital payments and a large incline in sophisticated management systems. Businesses embracing these technologies and raising customer experience shall be well-positioned in a growing marketplace."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/7e7af0_b26a4c6e5f684941a7ecfb726d07b61a~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/139(14-july-news-blog)%20(1).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-14', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('fine-dining-feels-the-pinch:-full-service-menus-see-bigger-price-jumps-than-fast-food', 'Fine Dining Feels the Pinch: Full-Service Menus See Bigger Price Jumps Than Fast Food', 'Unveiling the Booming Kiosk Market: Growth Drivers & Challenges', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Unveiling the Booming Kiosk Market: Growth Drivers & Challenges"},{"type":"p","text":"The Consumer Price Index fell 0.1% in June , the first drop since February 2020. It is up 3% from a year ago , the smallest year-over-year gain in 12 months, moving closer to the Federal Reserve''s 2% goal."},{"type":"p","text":"Inertia in Inflation Is Temporary: Optimist on Wall Street , Housing, Rent Prices Drive Cooling of Inflation"},{"type":"p","text":"Big contributors to this, though, were the falling prices of homes and rent. Food is a different story. New data received recently from the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics showed that the food index increased 0.2% in June, maintaining the robust advance of 0.1% in May. The cost of food at home, meanwhile, crept higher by 0.1% on the month while the food-away-from-home index swelled by 0.4%, matching the gain seen in May."},{"type":"p","text":"Food Price Changes Every Year"},{"type":"p","text":"The food-at-home index is up 1.1% year over year, vs. a 4.1% gain in restaurant prices. With the June-to-June advances, restaurant prices have been firm/rising more rapidly relative to grocery prices for 16 16-consecutive months since February 2015, and by 300 basis points. This spread has, on average, come in at 60 basis points, according to Kalinowski Equity Research."},{"type":"p","text":"Full-Service vs. Quick-Service Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"The June inflation index showed some eye-popping differences between full-service and quick-service restaurants. Prices for full-service restaurants advanced 0.6 percent in June, with prices for limited-service meals up just 0.2 percent. Full-service menu prices gained a bit more, building on a 0.4 percent increase in May and a 0.3 percent rise in April. Prices for limited-service meals were flat in June, and this offset May''s 0.2 percent gain while marking a slowdown from 0.4 percent in April, perhaps a real signal about the pressures of QSR value strategies."},{"type":"p","text":"Full-service meal prices are up 3.9 percent compared to a year ago, versus a 4.3 increase for limited-service menu prices. There is a more significant minimum wage hike impact in limited service, and it''s not driving a higher rate of increase versus full service."},{"type":"p","text":"Impact on Restaurant Industry Sales"},{"type":"p","text":"The prices between restaurants and grocery stores haven''t converged,\" according to Mark Kalinowski, chief executive and president of Kalinowski Equity Research. \"Consumers are now more price-sensitive and cook at home.\". One key aspect, he notes, is that, in 2016, when the gap extended out to 390 basis points, the restaurant industry notched the second-worst same-store sales performance in seven years, behind only the pandemic-impacted year."},{"type":"p","text":"Same-Store Sales Growth Forecast"},{"type":"p","text":"Now, Kalinowski claims that same-store sales growth will lie much weaker in the full year of 2024 compared to that of 2023. \"We continue to fully expect full-year 2024 same-store sales growth to be meaningfully lower than full-year 2023 same-store sales growth,\" Kalinowski wrote in a note. \"Full-year 2024 same-store sales growth will likely be the lowest - excluding pandemic-impacted 2020 - since 2018.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Consumer Behavior Shifts"},{"type":"p","text":"The persistent gap between restaurant and grocery prices would suggest, among other things, changing consumer behavior. If food, at home, is increasing but at a lower level than in restaurants, then consumers will shift more of food preparation to the home to control costs. This new behavior can affect the restaurant''s overall sales performance. That impact is already witnessed through the trends established over the recent past."},{"type":"p","text":"Final Verdict"},{"type":"p","text":"Worth noting, the slight decrease in the June Consumer Price Index, if it does come to pass, would be the first decrease in inflation since 2020. A portion of this drop has been cooled by house and rent price reductions, while aliquots for food remain worrisome. These wide chasms between full service and quick service, and restaurants versus grocery store prices for identical items, are setting consumer preference trends for a reduced sales growth trajectory in the Restaurant Industry. Through these changed times the industry will sail, and it shall be very capital-efficient in understanding and changing consumer behavior to maintain profitability and growth."},{"type":"p","text":"This will, therefore, put restaurant owners and managers at the forefront of such trends, strategizing on winning and retaining consumers going forward. Value offerings need balancing against quality service, especially in consideration of the critical role data insights are going to play in adjusting to the emerging conditions of the market."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/7e7af0_8f4af70ae1834b86bb5c7064802d9294~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/138-(13-julynews-blog)%20(1).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-13', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('the-future-is-self-serve:-kiosk-market-poised-for-explosive-growth,-hitting-$71-billion-in-2034', 'The Future is Self-Serve: Kiosk Market Poised for Explosive Growth, Hitting $71 Billion in 2034', 'Unveiling the Booming Kiosk Market: Growth Drivers & Challenges', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Unveiling the Booming Kiosk Market: Growth Drivers & Challenges"},{"type":"p","text":"According to Fact.MR, the latest updated research report claims that the kiosk market around the globe will be valued at US$ 29.45 billion in 2024 and will further progress with a CAGR of 9.2% through 2034."},{"type":"p","text":"Kiosks utilize the offers available to meet shopping needs with the help of an upselling tool. The kiosks allow the user to surf those products online and accordingly purchase the spot. It reduces the queueing, leading to an enhanced checkout experience."},{"type":"p","text":"The market for kiosks has been on the rise at a very fast rate as today''s customers like shopping at user-friendly places. This is in contrast to customers and end users in the market today who are always after faster and more convenient shopping due to their busy lives. As shown by the manufacturers, this has resulted in the incorporation of the latest technology and intelligent shopping processes into kiosks."},{"type":"p","text":"Machine Learning, Artificial Intelligence, the Internet of Things, and Wireless Internet connectivity add a lot of innovation to the kiosk manufacturers, and changes further strengthen the elements of giving the human face to connectivity. In the future, different kinds of Kiosks shall be used inside the premises for purposes like bill payments and helping passengers of the Public Transit."},{"type":"p","text":"The demand for product vending machines has been surging globally in coherence with everyday appliances, thus the ATM market. This has resulted in North America and East Asia maintaining the lead within regional markets with a combined share of around 60% in installed ATMs and POS terminals."},{"type":"p","text":"Important Market Takeaways from Fact.MR ''s Research"},{"type":"p","text":"The global kiosk market is expected to expand with a CAGR of 9.2% from 2024 to 2034. By the end of 2034, the market of kiosks is expected to go over $71.02 billion. In 2024, the US economy was projected to be worth US$ 8.05 billion."},{"type":"p","text":"The China market is pegged to capture a 48.9% market share in the East Asia market by 2024. Kiosk sales in Japan are pegged to reach US$ 1.87 bn by 2024. The North American market is likely to grow at a CAGR of 8.3% during the forecast period 2024-2034."},{"type":"p","text":"The demand for self-service and convenient access to services is growing in the market. Kiosks include artificial intelligence and machine learning, which provide increased predictive analytics and tailored experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"It is, therefore, logical that this type of activity remains in retail, hospitality, healthcare, and transportation through self-service options. Kiosks help such companies automate their transaction and other repetitive tasks, which will finally lead to output efficiency and cost reduction. Kiosks are automated even further with artificial intelligence and machine learning in place for the functionality of predictive analytics and improving user experiences. What this means is that kiosks will make viable suggestions in line with an individual''s choice."},{"type":"p","text":"The ongoing evolution of kiosks has been toward interfaces that are much more intuitive and user-friendly. To this end, user interfaces with enhanced touchscreens, interactive displays, and haptic and higher resolutions now come standard with ergonomic design."},{"type":"p","text":"The Expensive Infrastructure and Permits"},{"type":"p","text":"The high initial investment in the interactive kiosk and the continuous need for maintenance act as some of the challenges the self-service kiosk industry is facing. Expensive infrastructure and licensing are thus two primary factors that currently limit the growth of the market and adversely impact sales."},{"type":"p","text":"Now, by a hacker''s activity, it even becomes possible to expose data that is kiosk-sensitive: details of the financial instrument and customer contact information, among the rest of the reported personally identifiable information. Extra security for such devices is required, as this is an extremely easy target for hackers, which maintains steady growth in the market."},{"type":"p","text":"Country-Wise Insights"},{"type":"p","text":"North America is also projected to capture 38% part of the kiosk industry by 2024. Being the most urbanized and highly populated region, Asia has experienced dramatic growth in ATM deployment, especially in China, India, and Japan, among others. This fast growth can be largely attributed to the fast urbanization of Asian countries with high rates of population growth and increased demand for self-service service options."},{"type":"p","text":"Almost seventy-two percent of the North American region will be captured by the US by 2024, the reasons this company has remained at the helm of the market are the high availability of suppliers for digital kiosk display in the US and the early adopter of technology to lead the industry way back at the start of this century. The periods of major globalization, digitization, and the use of smart devices in almost all these industries are expected to drive this market into rapid growth shortly as well."},{"type":"p","text":"Sales of kiosks in China are growing at a fast pace due to the country''s expanding tourism industry. There is a much higher demand in China for ATM kiosks because most people there are switching to smart ATMs that already have interactive touch screens. The market is also set to grow as further innovations, like speech-to-text and other smartphone integrations, take off over the coming years. Chinese consumers are getting used to technology and comfortable dealing with companies online. Several customers appreciate speed and convenience, either for every order made at a pay station, when ordering take-out or for doing bank transactions or activities such as buying tickets."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/7e7af0_cb5fecd8b0c54871beceb62b9850229f~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/137(12-july-news)%20(1).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-12', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('beyond-meals-on-wheels:-the-tech-driven-future-of-senior-care-dining', 'Beyond Meals on Wheels: The Tech-Driven Future of Senior Care Dining', 'Meals on Wheels is Just the Beginning: Are You Ready for the Future of Senior Dining?', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Meals on Wheels is Just the Beginning: Are You Ready for the Future of Senior Dining?"},{"type":"p","text":"Technology is transforming every aspect of senior care communities, from healthcare to social activities. But have you considered how it''s also revolutionizing the dining experience? Yes, even mealtimes are getting a high-tech makeover, thanks to innovative solutions that streamline operations and enhance the overall enjoyment for residents."},{"type":"p","text":"Tech on the Menu: A Taste of What''s Possible"},{"type":"p","text":"Senior care communities are embracing a variety of tech tools to elevate their dining programs:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Smart Menus & Ordering: No more static menus! Residents can now browse digital menus, customize their orders, and even place them from the comfort of their own rooms. This means faster service, less food waste, and meals tailored to individual preferences.","Inventory & Purchasing Power: Say goodbye to overstocked freezers and last-minute grocery runs. AI-powered systems can track inventory in real-time, predict demand, and even automate ordering, ensuring a well-stocked kitchen and a wider variety of meal choices.","Nutrition on Point: Dietary needs are crucial in senior care. Digital systems can instantly access resident profiles, flagging allergies, preferences, and restrictions to ensure safe and satisfying meals for everyone."]},{"type":"p","text":"Benefits for Residents, Staff, and the Bottom Line"},{"type":"p","text":"Why are senior care communities embracing dining technology? The benefits are clear:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Happier Residents: Personalized menus, faster service, and the ability to order anytime, anywhere create a more enjoyable and empowering dining experience.","Less Stress for Staff: By automating tedious tasks, staff can focus on what matters most: building relationships with residents and providing top-notch service.","Healthier Outcomes: Technology can track nutritional intake, identify potential deficiencies, and even suggest personalized meal plans, contributing to better overall health for residents.","Reduced Costs: Optimizing inventory, minimizing waste, and streamlining operations all contribute to a more efficient and cost-effective dining program."]},{"type":"p","text":"Recipe for Success: Tips for Implementation"},{"type":"p","text":"Ready to give your dining program a tech upgrade? Here are some key steps:"},{"type":"p","text":"1. Assess Your Needs: Identify the specific pain points in your current dining operations. Are you struggling with long wait times, menu planning, or dietary restrictions?"},{"type":"p","text":"2. Choose the Right Tools: Research different technologies and find solutions that address your specific needs and budget. Don''t hesitate to ask for demos or trial periods."},{"type":"p","text":"3. Get Staff on Board: Provide comprehensive training and support for your staff. Their buy-in is crucial for successful implementation."},{"type":"p","text":"4. Communicate with Residents: Explain the benefits of the new technology to residents and offer ongoing support as they adapt."},{"type":"p","text":"The Future of Dining is Now"},{"type":"p","text":"The future of senior care dining is undeniably digital. From AI-powered menus to smart kitchen appliances, technology is transforming the way we approach mealtime. By embracing these innovations, senior care communities can create a more personalized, enjoyable, and nutritious dining experience for their residents."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_667b198272cd4a74afd2426c45e889ff~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/image%20(23).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-11', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('technology''s-impact-on-reducing-food-costs-and-minimizing-waste-in-restaurants', 'Technology''s Impact on Reducing Food Costs and Minimizing Waste in Restaurants', 'Industry Shift: Restaurants Embrace Tech to Combat Inflation and Labor Woes', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Industry Shift: Restaurants Embrace Tech to Combat Inflation and Labor Woes"},{"type":"p","text":"Labor costs are on the rise, particularly in markets with a higher minimum wage than $15 an hour, and rising ingredient costs feed into menu pricing. Indeed, according to the National Restaurant Association, menu prices have increased by 4.1% over the past 12 months."},{"type":"p","text":"Accordingly, restaurants are promptly investing in smart technology that will help them save labor and trim food costs by relying on loyalty programs and saving more to do more with less."},{"type":"p","text":"Operations Are Made Simpler by Smart Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Providing the best value for the experience is essential while managing narrow margins. Accuracy in the cost of products sold can be increased and errors can be decreased with the use of real-time data. Team members can see where deficiencies are due to information updates on sales and product amounts provided via real-time inventory access. This improves the restaurant''s efficiency and helps it adapt to changing customer preferences in the future."},{"type":"p","text":"Businesses such as Sbarro use this intelligent technology to evaluate efficiency and profitability trends across several sites and use insights to make critical business choices in real-time and increase return on investment. By eliminating the need for manual reporting and saving franchises a substantial amount of time, intelligent technology frees up personnel to concentrate on the client experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Handheld gadgets can expedite procedures and lower the number of cashiers required to process orders in quick service. Staff at the drive-thru enter the lane, take orders quickly, and move quickly, as Chick-fil-A and In-N-Out have demonstrated for a long time."},{"type":"p","text":"Consider loyalty"},{"type":"p","text":"Cost-conscious consumers are aware of ways to save money in light of the present inflation rate; as a result, up to 50% of them enroll in digital loyalty programs. The way that people view loyalty is changing. Customers now view these programs as essential, whereas formerly they were thought of as a good bonus. The brands they choose to frequent can be determined by the accumulation and use of points."},{"type":"p","text":"To take advantage of repeat business and promote revenue development, restaurants are responding by increasing their investments in loyalty programs and offering customized incentives and offers. Restaurants of all sizes, not just chains, need to think about implementing a digital loyalty infrastructure that allows for infinite expansion and flexibility, allowing them to easily roll out programs and try new things without running into operational or technological roadblocks."},{"type":"p","text":"About 8 million people are members of the International Bank of Pancakes (IBOP) loyalty program, which was established by the International House of Pancakes in 2022. There are over 8,000 downloads of the IHOP loyalty app every day, and members visit the restaurant twice as frequently and spend almost 5% more than non-members."},{"type":"p","text":"While discounts for money spent are emphasized in many brand loyalty programs, programs are starting to focus more on individualized rewards. In addition, loyalty programs are being added by full-service restaurants more frequently than quick-serve/fast-casual chains to increase sales and encourage return business."},{"type":"p","text":"Reduce the Cost of Food and More"},{"type":"p","text":"One restaurant may produce from 25,000 to 75,000 pounds of food waste in one year. Food waste is a major area of potential savings when a restaurateur is tossing out the perishables before they have had a chance to use them. The inventory control software can alert kitchen staff when certain items are nearing their \"best used by\" date and can even help them figure out when to rotate stock."},{"type":"p","text":"However, reducing food waste and optimizing your back-office processes won''t decrease costs by themselves. Restaurants can examine their current menu items closely and use innovative menu planning to optimize food expenses."},{"type":"p","text":"Use sophisticated technology to perform a menu audit that can distinguish between areas of concern, which are products that are costly, complicated to manufacture, and either popular or not, and the holy grail menu items, which are inexpensive, simple to make, and extremely popular. Restaurants may focus on the proper dishes and streamline their menu with the help of an audit, providing customers with consistently high-quality meals that will encourage repeat business."},{"type":"p","text":"In addition to streamlining their menu, eateries ought also to think about doing away with their printed menus completely. Make the move to digital menu boards, iPads, or self-ordering kiosks; staff can concentrate on providing additional value-added services to consumers and these are less expensive and easier to update. These technologies can also improve the client experience by providing customized menus and food recommendations."},{"type":"p","text":"Increase Productivity While Decreasing Waste"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants need to find strategies to survive and grow in the face of inflation, which includes rising food prices, and rising labor costs. This requires the use of intelligent technology. This entails making use of mobile devices, loyalty plans, menu audits, inventory management systems, QR codes, and other technology designed specifically for restaurants."},{"type":"p","text":"You can do more with less when you use technology. Having the appropriate platform or platforms can mean the difference between your brand succeeding and simply scraping by in a challenging environment."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/7e7af0_d70f787ae2b54997b5a5fcc5a18a9abf~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/image%20(2).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-10', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('earn-and-learn:-walmart-&-mcdonald''s-offer-college-credit-for-work-experience', 'Earn and Learn: Walmart & McDonald''s Offer College Credit for Work Experience', 'In a groundbreaking move, major corporations like Walmart and McDonald''s are exploring a new frontier in higher education. They are collaborating with colleges to award college credits to their employees for skills acqui', '[{"type":"h2","text":"College Degree While Working? Walmart & McDonald''s Make it Possible"},{"type":"p","text":"In a groundbreaking move, major corporations like Walmart and McDonald''s are exploring a new frontier in higher education. They are collaborating with colleges to award college credits to their employees for skills acquired on the job, challenging the traditional notion that a college degree is the sole path to career advancement."},{"type":"p","text":"The Rationale Behind the Shift"},{"type":"p","text":"This shift stems from several key realizations:"},{"type":"ul","items":["College Degrees as Imperfect Proxies: A diploma doesn''t always accurately reflect a person''s knowledge and skills.","High Cost of Education: The exorbitant cost of higher education excludes many talented individuals.","Industry Needs: Industries dominated by workers without degrees need to find innovative ways to cultivate talent."]},{"type":"p","text":"A New Vision for Hiring"},{"type":"p","text":"Executives envision a future where resumes focus less on academic credentials and more on proven skills. By awarding college credit for on-the-job learning, companies are paving the way for a more inclusive and accessible education system."},{"type":"p","text":"Challenges and Opportunities"},{"type":"p","text":"While the concept is promising, there are challenges to overcome. Determining how much college credit a work skill is worth remains a complex task."},{"type":"p","text":"Walmart''s Pioneering Efforts"},{"type":"p","text":"Walmart has taken the lead with its \"Walmart Academy,\" offering training programs and certifications that translate to college credit. This initiative aims to provide employees with a pathway to earn up to half of a college degree through their work experience."},{"type":"p","text":"McDonald''s Pilot Program"},{"type":"p","text":"McDonald''s is partnering with community colleges to explore how on-the-job skills, such as food safety and customer service, can be converted into college credit for culinary arts, hospitality, or insurance degrees."},{"type":"p","text":"Expanding Access and Opportunities"},{"type":"p","text":"Educators hope this trend will increase access to education, allowing more individuals to pursue better-paying careers with less debt. Companies see it as a way to attract and retain talent, reduce turnover, and cultivate loyalty."},{"type":"p","text":"Lessons from the Military"},{"type":"p","text":"The U.S. military has successfully implemented a system for awarding college credit for military training and experience. This model serves as inspiration for the corporate world''s efforts to recognize and reward on-the-job learning."},{"type":"p","text":"The Road Ahead: A Skills-First Approach"},{"type":"p","text":"The future of higher education may involve a shift towards a \"skills-first approach,\" where short-form certificates and credentials hold equal weight with traditional degrees. This approach could revolutionize how we value work experience and open up new pathways for career advancement."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_e8168929dedd4ba2a5acd344b80a4034~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/130(09-07-24-newblog).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-09', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('mapping-the-market:-investor-moves-in-restaurant-technology', 'Mapping the Market: Investor Moves in Restaurant Technology', 'Investors Sustain Interest in Restaurant Tech Amidst Flat Foodtech Deal Flow', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Investors Sustain Interest in Restaurant Tech Amidst Flat Foodtech Deal Flow"},{"type":"p","text":"Investors seem to have had enough of foodtech. VC investment in the vertical has remained stagnant over the past six quarters, according to PitchBook data, hovering between $1.96 billion and $2.16 billion in quarterly deal value. Q1 2024 saw $2.2 billion invested across 246 deals, a slight uptick from the previous quarter."},{"type":"p","text":"This steady investment pattern indicates that the sector is maturing from its explosive growth patterns to a more stable phase. That means investors are adopting a more wait-and-see attitude, very astutely picking opportunities that yield steady results rather than high-risk, high-reward strategies. At the same time, stability points out a solid base and continued interest in foodtech, driven by ongoing innovations and the essential nature of industries having to do with food."},{"type":"p","text":"Continued Interest in Restaurant and Retail Tech"},{"type":"p","text":"But investors aren''t dining and dashing entirely. Restaurant and retail tech, technologies and services that improve cooking precision and effectiveness, cut down waste, and help track food, has continued to attract fresh funding. This sector remains a bright spot within the foodtech vertical."},{"type":"p","text":"Market Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"PitchBook customers can view the full market map, complete with details on more than 7,900 companies. This enables investors to identify trends, benchmark performance, and understand where an opportunity sits within the dynamic landscape of restaurant and retail tech."},{"type":"p","text":"Spotlight: Restaurant and Retail Tech Categories"},{"type":"p","text":"The retail tech segment is broken into six categories by the PitchBook analysts:"},{"type":"p","text":"Advanced Vending"},{"type":"p","text":"Independent robotic food and beverage distributors, such as contactless restaurants or vending machines. These technologies are quickly becoming very popular among a host of consumers who want quick and contactless service."},{"type":"p","text":"Delivery Robots"},{"type":"p","text":"Autonomous machines that deliver groceries and takeout. These robots revolutionize the last mile of delivery, reducing labor costs and increasing the speed and reliability of food delivery services."},{"type":"p","text":"Ghost Kitchens"},{"type":"p","text":"Commercial kitchens that service meal delivery platforms without providing brick-and-mortar dining experiences. Ghost kitchens respond to growing interest in food delivery and seek ways to increase a restaurant''s presence without having a traditional restaurant setup."},{"type":"p","text":"Grocery Store Tech"},{"type":"p","text":"Food retail and grocery store-oriented robot and software services, from checkout automation to inventory management tools and robotic stocking, enhance the efficiency and customer experience of grocery stores."},{"type":"p","text":"Kitchen Tech and Robotics"},{"type":"p","text":"Automation technologies designed for use in kitchen environments, these technologies combat labor constraints and health risks. From robotic culinary experts to automated dishwashers, these solutions make kitchen operations much safer and more efficient."},{"type":"p","text":"Sales and Operations Tech"},{"type":"p","text":"A solution specifically developed by restaurants to manage their inventories, points of sale, and customer loyalty at the drive-through. These products are cornerstones in the modern management of restaurants, having helped owners reduce their waste, streamline their operations, and delight their customers."},{"type":"p","text":"Flat Deal Flow, Historic Setting"},{"type":"p","text":"Foodtech deal flow has been relatively flat for a year and a half. All in all, 2023 continued that decline, hosting 1,339 deals for $9.6 billion, far from the vertical''s peak in 2021 when it generated $47 billion from 2,250 deals. Much of this decline can be credited to a mix of market saturation, economic uncertainty, and a general refocus by investors toward more mature and stable opportunities."},{"type":"p","text":"While these sustained levels of investment are indicative that the sector is no longer growing at the exhilarating rates it used to, it''s an important and ongoing area for innovation and investment. The continued funding also shows just how in-demand technological change within the food industry remains as it grapples with labor shortages, supply chain disruption, and shifting consumer preferences."},{"type":"p","text":"Q1 2024 Performance"},{"type":"p","text":"A restaurant- and retail-tech segment raised $551.5 million in Q1 2024 to become the second-best-performing vertical in the space. Such notable rounds as $388 million in growth funding for Dutch online grocery Picnic a month ago, $90 million for precision fermentation Perfect Day in January, and the mammoth $665 million round for Indian online grocery store Zepto in June were all announced."},{"type":"p","text":"The landing of these huge investments thus attests to the surge in the need for technological solutions within the increasingly competitive food industry. Companies like Picnic and Zepto are scaling their operations, improving customer experience, and growing their business with technology. Ample funding rounds suggest that investors retain much faith in these companies to shake up traditional models of food retail and delivery."},{"type":"p","text":"Analysis of the Exit Environment"},{"type":"p","text":"As generally occurred for most VC landscapes, the exit environment remained muted for foodtech from its peak: $104.9 billion raised across 119 deals in 2021; Q1 2024: $100m in exit value across 18 deals; Notable exits include meal kit delivery service Blue Apron''s buy by Wonder in November for $103 million. In April, frozen food giant McCain Foods agreed to acquire plant-based frozen foods manufacturer Strong Roots for an undisclosed amount."},{"type":"p","text":"Subdued exit activity is illustrative of how far foodtech startups have gone without seeing a liquidity event, but some notable exits do indicate strategic interest in foodtech assets. The value proposition of firms like Blue Apron and Strong Roots, which gives a clear proposition of convenience, health, and sustainability, endows them with a special place in the eyes of probable acquirers."},{"type":"p","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"While the general landscape of investment in foodtech has been flat, certain segments, like restaurant and retail technologies, have continued to show deep investor interest. These technologies inherently drive industry efficiency and innovation, making for compelling investment opportunities. For a fuller exposition of these trends and much more, PitchBook''s Q1 2024 Foodtech Report contains important insight and data."},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant and retail tech sectors have retained huge interest and investment due to their critical role in shaping the future of Food Service and Retail. As companies find ways to innovate and adapt to changing market conditions, investors will more than likely find enough opportunities to support transformative technologies that will enhance operational efficiency, meet consumer demand, and develop growth prospects for the food sector."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/bcb0b2_bcf8b01eeadb485a87321ec2fdd04bf2~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/blog%20img.png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-08', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('invest-in-your-future:-how-a-custom-tech-stack-can-transform-your-restaurant', 'Invest in Your Future: How a Custom Tech Stack Can Transform Your Restaurant', 'Ever walked into a beautifully designed restaurant only to be met with a frustratingly slow ordering process? It''s a common scenario that highlights the growing disconnect between aesthetics and functionality in the dini', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Is Your Tech Holding You Back? Discover the Power of a Tailored Solution Benefit"},{"type":"p","text":"Ever walked into a beautifully designed restaurant only to be met with a frustratingly slow ordering process? It''s a common scenario that highlights the growing disconnect between aesthetics and functionality in the dining experience. This friction is even more pronounced in the digital realm, where customers expect seamless, user-friendly ordering. Failing to invest in streamlined ordering solutions puts brands at a significant disadvantage, risking lost customers and revenue."},{"type":"p","text":"Beyond One-Size-Fits-All"},{"type":"p","text":"Generic ordering platforms may seem convenient, but they rarely cater to a brand''s unique personality and operational needs. To thrive, restaurants need to adopt tailored digital ordering solutions that optimize revenue-driving operations - from menu management and pricing to data analysis. This is no longer optional; it''s essential for survival in the digital age."},{"type":"p","text":"The Stats Speak Volumes"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants underinvesting in digital are missing out. According to BackofHouse.io, 97% of customers use at least one online ordering platform, but 70% of restaurants rate their existing tech stacks as \"poor\" or \"fair.\" These numbers are a wake-up call. Every outdated or impersonal interaction pushes customers closer to competitors who offer a more frictionless experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Future-Proofing Through Constant Evolution"},{"type":"p","text":"A great tech partner goes beyond solving current problems. They proactively evolve their solutions to meet future demands, leveraging industry experience and transaction data to anticipate customer needs and adapt to macro trends. Customization is key, not just in branding, but in tailoring the entire digital experience to reflect the brand''s identity and operational nuances."},{"type":"p","text":"Seamless Integration is Critical"},{"type":"p","text":"The best tech partners ensure their platforms seamlessly integrate with existing restaurant software. Clunky integrations hinder operational efficiency and create training nightmares for staff who must learn disparate systems. True future-proofing demands flexibility at every level, from menu updates and smart upsells to centralized pricing controls and bulk data management."},{"type":"p","text":"The Right Partner Amplifies Your Vision"},{"type":"p","text":"No one knows your brand better than you do. The right tech partner understands this and collaborates to translate your vision into a best-in-class digital experience. They''ll take the time to understand your business''s nuances, pain points, and goals, offering hands-on support to ensure their technology works seamlessly with your operations."},{"type":"p","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"In today''s landscape, online and in-person dining are intertwined. Embracing tailored digital solutions is crucial for restaurants to control their narrative, drive sales, and deliver exceptional customer experiences. It''s time to serve up an ordering platform as unique and memorable as your food."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_83f3bcec636f4ccab447bbd9b1d04e08~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_3000,h_2000,al_c,q_90/124(6june-news)%20(1).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-06', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('controlling-kitchen-chaos:-how-restaurant-technologies-can-help', 'Controlling Kitchen Chaos: How Restaurant Technologies Can Help', 'Taming the Kitchen Beast: Technology''s Role in Restaurant Efficiency', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Taming the Kitchen Beast: Technology''s Role in Restaurant Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"As the foodservice industry grapples with escalating operating expenses nationwide, finding ways to manage costs and maintain profitability has become crucial. One effective approach is to identify and capitalize on hidden savings opportunities that often go unnoticed. By implementing innovative strategies such as automating cooking oil processes and flue cleaning, foodservice businesses can significantly reduce labor costs, insurance premiums, and enhance overall kitchen efficiency."},{"type":"p","text":"Safety, Labor Efficiency, and Employee Retention"},{"type":"p","text":"Managing hot cooking oil is a notoriously dangerous and unpleasant task in commercial kitchens. It poses risks of burns and slip-and-fall accidents, and employees often dread the tedious process of filtering cooking oil. By automating oil management, foodservice businesses can eliminate one of the most hazardous and undesirable jobs, leading to improved employee morale, a more positive work environment, and increased staff retention."},{"type":"p","text":"TJ Ahmed, owner of Spring Valley Jack, LLC, a multi-brand franchisee company operating five Jack in the Box restaurants in Texas, experienced firsthand the challenges of manual oil management. He witnessed employees getting burned by grease, oil spills causing cleaning hassles, and difficulties associated with handling grease drums. Implementing automated solutions has transformed his kitchen operations."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurant Technologies'' Total Oil Management® and AutoMist® solutions have been recognized for their contributions to safety and efficiency, receiving numerous industry awards, including the Buyer''s Edge 2023 Labor Saving Solution of the Year award."},{"type":"p","text":"Controlled Claims and Insurance Costs"},{"type":"p","text":"Automated oil management significantly reduces the risks of costly accidents, such as burns and slips from spilled oil. Additionally, automated hood and flue cleaning systems help prevent grease buildup, mitigating the risk of fires. By minimizing these risks, foodservice businesses can potentially achieve substantial reductions in insurance costs."},{"type":"p","text":"Savings in Oil Usage and Improved Food Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"Automated oil replacement eliminates guesswork, ensuring optimal oil usage and preventing premature or delayed replacements that can lead to waste or compromised food quality. Customers have reported significant savings by maximizing oil life without sacrificing the taste and quality of their fried foods."},{"type":"p","text":"Jeff Lingel, area manager at Apple American Group, the largest Applebee''s franchisee with over 300 restaurants, emphasizes the benefits of the fryer filtration monitoring system in optimizing oil maintenance and extending oil life. This, in turn, enhances the quality of their fried food offerings."},{"type":"p","text":"Enhanced Customer Satisfaction"},{"type":"p","text":"Maintaining consistent oil quality results in consistently delicious menu items, attracting repeat customers and helping offset rising labor expenses. Implementing Total Oil Management and AutoMist creates a win-win scenario for businesses, staff, and customers alike."},{"type":"p","text":"Key Takeaways:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Rising foodservice costs demand innovative solutions for cost management.","Automating cooking oil processes and flue cleaning offers significant hidden savings.","Enhanced safety, improved labor efficiency, and reduced insurance costs are key benefits.","Automated oil management optimizes oil usage, enhances food quality, and boosts customer satisfaction."]},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_2791171051a94d208c7406104b76211c~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/122(04-july-news-)%20(1).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-05', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('the-roi-of-smart-signage:-how-ai-powered-drive-thrus-drive-revenue-growth', 'The ROI of Smart Signage: How AI-Powered Drive-Thrus Drive Revenue Growth', 'Upselling Made Easy: Smart Signage Suggests Add-ons and Upgrades', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Upselling Made Easy: Smart Signage Suggests Add-ons and Upgrades"},{"type":"p","text":"With the rise of off-premises dining, the quick-service restaurant (QSR) segment is seeing a significant shift in revenue generation. This trend has brought state-of-the-art signage to the forefront, transforming drive-thrus and pickup areas. Effective signage not only addresses common challenges like poor traffic flow and inconsistent branding but also enhances the overall customer experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Investing in Drive-Thrus and Off-Premises Dining"},{"type":"p","text":"In 2024, QSR operators are actively investing in upgrading or adding drive-thrus, walk-up windows, and technology to streamline off-premises dining. The emphasis on speed and efficiency has led to a new mantra in the industry: \"Seconds matter.\" According to Robert Creasy, vice president of business development for DSA Signage, managing high volumes of drive-thru, online, and delivery orders requires a constant focus on balancing throughput, speed, efficiency, customer service, and communication."},{"type":"p","text":"Adapting to Change with Digital Signage"},{"type":"p","text":"Drive-thru renovations are now occurring every three to five years due to advancements in technology and the need for more lanes. This has spurred the demand for both static and digital signage solutions to accommodate multiple lanes and separate pickup areas. Digital menuboards, in particular, have become increasingly important as menu prices fluctuate. Their ability to quickly and easily update food offerings and prices makes them invaluable for QSRs facing a dynamic market."},{"type":"p","text":"Balancing Cost and Functionality"},{"type":"p","text":"The choice between static and digital menus is a key consideration for QSR operators. While digital signage offers flexibility and dynamic pricing updates, static signage often comes with a lower upfront cost. Large, backlit static and digital menuboards enhance visibility in various lighting conditions and can be used strategically to promote high-margin items and encourage impulse sales."},{"type":"p","text":"Future Trends: Automation and Digitalization"},{"type":"p","text":"The industry is expected to see continued growth in automation and digitalization to address challenges like inflation and rising labor costs. Self-service kiosks and AI-powered menu boards, already popular in some European markets, are anticipated to gain traction in the US. These technologies promise to further optimize traffic flow, improve customer service, and reduce operational expenses for QSRs."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_7f6da41faf844335a78d4aad963bd426~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/120(04-july-news).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-04', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('minimum-wage-laws:-a-blessing-in-disguise-for-the-kiosk-industry?', 'Minimum Wage Laws: A Blessing in Disguise for the Kiosk Industry?', 'How Higher Wages Could Drive a Boom in Self-Service Kiosks', '[{"type":"h2","text":"How Higher Wages Could Drive a Boom in Self-Service Kiosks"},{"type":"p","text":"Progressive activists have sought to protect workers from exploitation through minimum wages and workplace regulations, seeking to curb the heartless and brutal exploitation inherent in the capitalist system, as described by Karl Marx and those he influenced. In their view, history is a story of class struggle between capital-owning exploiters and the working class. However, a closer look reveals a more complex reality where these well-intentioned rules often have unintended consequences."},{"type":"p","text":"Minimum Wage: Protection or Substitution?"},{"type":"p","text":"While these regulations aim to protect workers, they often benefit those who can substitute for low-skill labor. The moving company \"Two Men and a Truck\" illustrates this point. Without minimum wage laws and regulations, they might employ teenagers, offering more job opportunities. However, these rules make teen labor costly, leading to fewer jobs and less consumer choice."},{"type":"p","text":"The Rise of the Machines"},{"type":"p","text":"Another unintended beneficiary is the automation industry. Higher minimum wages incentivize businesses like fast-food restaurants to adopt labor-saving technologies like ordering kiosks and apps. As Jacob Vigdor noted in an EconTalk episode, once developed, these technologies can be easily deployed elsewhere, regardless of local minimum wage levels. This means that even regions with lower minimum wages may experience job losses due to automation."},{"type":"p","text":"Economic Incentives and the Search for Substitutes"},{"type":"p","text":"Economics teaches us that when something gets more expensive, people seek alternatives. This applies to labor as well. When low-skill labor becomes costlier due to minimum wages or regulations, businesses seek substitutes, like automation or higher-skilled labor. This can reduce opportunities for those the regulations were intended to help."},{"type":"p","text":"Historical Parallels"},{"type":"p","text":"The unintended consequences of minimum wages are not new. As Thomas Leonard''s book \"Illiberal Reformers\" shows, early proponents of such regulations understood they would disproportionately harm the least well-off, particularly immigrants and African Americans. These laws effectively priced them out of the labor market. Similar dynamics played out in South Africa, where \"rate for the job\" laws (minimum wages) protected white workers from competition."},{"type":"p","text":"Who Benefits?"},{"type":"p","text":"While well-intentioned, minimum wage laws often benefit those they aren''t designed for. Instead of helping low-skill workers, they often enrich higher-skill workers, software developers, and shareholders in automation companies. Voters who support these laws with the aim of assisting vulnerable workers may unknowingly be contributing to a different outcome."},{"type":"p","text":"Conclusion: A Complex Reality"},{"type":"p","text":"The impact of minimum wage laws is more nuanced than the traditional Marxist narrative suggests. While aiming to protect workers, these laws can inadvertently harm those they intend to help by limiting job opportunities, accelerating automation, and benefiting higher-skilled workers. A deeper understanding of these complexities is crucial for crafting effective labor policies."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_ab41c1612e0245b7ac0091f4f1a5ab96~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/118(2june-news-room).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-03', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('california''s-junk-fee-law-spares-restaurant-surcharges', 'California''s Junk Fee Law Spares Restaurant Surcharges', 'Hidden Fees Under Fire, But Your Favorite Restaurant is Safe', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Hidden Fees Under Fire, But Your Favorite Restaurant is Safe"},{"type":"p","text":"California restaurants can breathe a sigh of relief as they are now officially exempt from the state''s new junk fee law, which went into effect on July 1st. Governor Gavin Newsom signed the exemption bill, SB 1524, just two days before the ban was set to begin."},{"type":"p","text":"What Does the Exemption Mean?"},{"type":"p","text":"While the original junk fee law, SB 478, aimed to eliminate hidden fees and surcharges not included in the initial price given to consumers, the exemption specifically allows restaurants to continue adding service charges and gratuities to bills. However, this comes with a crucial requirement: restaurants must be transparent and disclose these fees upfront."},{"type":"p","text":"No More Surprise Charges"},{"type":"p","text":"The exemption mandates that restaurants clearly display any service charges or fees on their menus, advertisements, or other displays where food or beverage prices are listed. This means no more unexpected additions to your bill at the end of your meal."},{"type":"p","text":"Balancing Transparency and Industry Concerns"},{"type":"p","text":"The last-minute exemption was crafted in response to concerns raised by the restaurant industry about the potential negative impact of the junk fee ban on workers and small businesses. State Senator Bill Dodd, who introduced the exemption, emphasized the importance of maintaining price transparency for consumers while protecting the interests of the food service industry."},{"type":"p","text":"Key Points for Restaurants"},{"type":"ul","items":["Clear Disclosure: Restaurants must clearly state any service charges or fees, along with an explanation of their purpose, on all relevant materials.","Timeframe: Businesses have one year from the implementation of the law to ensure compliance with the disclosure requirements.","Broad Application: The exemption applies to a wide range of food service businesses, including restaurants, bars, food concessions, grocery stores, grocery delivery services, banquets, and catering services."]},{"type":"p","text":"Industry Support"},{"type":"p","text":"The California Restaurant Association has expressed support for the exemption, recognizing its importance in providing clarity for businesses and consumers alike."},{"type":"p","text":"What''s Next?"},{"type":"p","text":"While this exemption provides a welcome reprieve for restaurants, it remains to be seen how it will impact consumer behavior and the overall dining experience in California. As the industry adapts to the new rules, diners can expect greater transparency and a more predictable billing process."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_074a611d0ed745889f7265deda2d101c~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1055,al_c/image%20(21).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-07-02', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('new-safety-standards-for-california''s-workers-as-heatwaves-intensify', 'New Safety Standards for California''s Workers as Heatwaves Intensify', 'Keeping Workers Safe in Rising Temperatures.', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Keeping Workers Safe in Rising Temperatures."},{"type":"p","text":"Following the state''s first dangerous heatwave of 2024, California has implemented new standards set to protect restaurant kitchen staff and other workers who labor indoors in what can be, at times, blistering conditions. Announced Thursday, the new regulations will require businesses to take protective measures when indoor temperatures hit more than 87 degrees Fahrenheit."},{"type":"p","text":"Changes in Regulations for Indoor Workplaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Under new proposed changes, businesses must ensure that workplaces are not cooled to no more than 87 degrees \"if feasible.\" For those workers in protective clothing and who deal with high-heat-producing machinery like stoves and ovens, the maximum limit will be pegged at below 82 degrees. Other measures include employers being required to provide access to water, \"cool-down areas,\" and rest breaks to help mitigate the effects of excessive heat."},{"type":"p","text":"Details of the New Standards"},{"type":"p","text":"The state Occupational Safety and Health Standards Board, the same board that unveiled those changes, did not speak to what circumstances might render cooling measures infeasible, though the regulations do single out restaurant kitchens as being uniquely indoors and in need of such additional protections."},{"type":"p","text":"Process for Approval and Implementation"},{"type":"p","text":"The revised employer requirements should be submitted for the review of regulatory changes to the state''s Office of Administrative Law within 30 business days for approval or rejection. The OSHSB asked that the requirements be operative immediately upon approval by the Administrative Law Office."},{"type":"p","text":"Heatwave Warnings and Broader Impact"},{"type":"p","text":"These regulatory updates come at a time when meteorologists have warned about triple-digit temperatures in parts of California. Last weekend, a record-breaking area stretching as far as Vermont was similarly scorching."},{"type":"p","text":"Growing Attention to Heat Safety on the Job"},{"type":"p","text":"Dangerous heat in the workplace has grown as a point of increasing focus by safety officials and organized labor as temperatures smash records. Preliminary data for 2023 tallies 2,030 heat-related deaths in the United States, the highest count in the last 45 years such data has been tracked. That is a significant rise from 1,600 fatalities in 2021 and 1,722 in 2022, according to the U.S. Health & Human Services Department. This includes all heat-related deaths, not only those at workplaces."},{"type":"p","text":"Federal Efforts to Combat Workplace Heat"},{"type":"p","text":"Nearly three years ago the White House ordered the U.S. Department of Labor to revise federal Occupational Safety & Health Administration, or OSHA, standards to better protect workers from excessive heat. To that end, a proposed set of federal safeguards is under review by the White House Office of Information and Regulatory Affairs."},{"type":"p","text":"Recap of proposed new heat standards"},{"type":"p","text":"California has enacted new regulations requiring employers to protect indoor workers, particularly restaurant kitchen staff and others who work in extremely hot conditions. Employers must now take protective action when indoor temperatures rise higher than 87 degrees. This includes: cooling the workspace to no more than 87 degrees when feasible; or, to as low as 82 degrees when employees must wear protective clothing or work near radiant heat sources. In addition, employers are mandated to provide access to water, cool-down areas, and rest breaks."},{"type":"p","text":"Information on Feasibility and Affected Workplaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Although the OSHSB did not elaborate on any conditions under which cooling measures would be deemed infeasible, restaurant kitchens have been especially singled out as one of the kinds of workplaces to be positively impacted by this regulation."},{"type":"p","text":"Timeline for Review and Approval"},{"type":"p","text":"The Office of Administrative Law has 30 business days to review the new standards. The OSHSB has requested that the measures be put into effect immediately upon approval."},{"type":"p","text":"Broader Heatwave Impact and Safety Focus"},{"type":"p","text":"With meteorologists predicting triple-digit temperatures in parts of California, and much of the country baking last weekend, an already heightened focus takes place on workplace heat safety. The record heat brought increased scrutiny from safety officials and labor organizations."},{"type":"p","text":"Alarming Statistics on Heat-Related Fatalities"},{"type":"p","text":"In 2022, the United States broke a record with 2,030 heat-related illness deaths, the highest in 45 years. There were 1,600 deaths in 2021, while this year the death count rose to 1,722, prompting alarm over an ominous trend of extreme heat."},{"type":"p","text":"Federal Action on Heat Safety Standards"},{"type":"p","text":"Amid escalating heat dangers, nearly three years ago, the White House ordered the U.S. Department of Labor to update OSHA standards. Proposed federal protections were submitted to the White House Office of Information and Regulatory Affairs for review."},{"type":"p","text":"To Sum Up"},{"type":"p","text":"California''s new standards for the protection of indoor workers from excessive heat reflect a growing awareness of the dangers posed by extreme temperatures. At the same time, as the state waits to see these regulations approved and implemented, this broad effort of improvement in workplace safety in the face of rising temperatures remains a critical issue nationwide."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_1a765c95a613400382b74b72c6dbbdb3~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/image%20(21).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-28', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('dubai''s-krasota-restaurant-revives-legendary-chef-with-ai-for-a-unique-dining-experience', 'Dubai''s Krasota Restaurant Revives Legendary Chef with AI for a Unique Dining Experience', 'The Future of Food: Dubai''s AI-Powered Restaurant', '[{"type":"h2","text":"The Future of Food: Dubai''s AI-Powered Restaurant"},{"type":"p","text":"Located in the fine dining area of Dubai, Krasota epitomizes how frontier technologies like Artificial Intelligence are extending the horizons of culinary innovation; the great restaurant features multisensory dining in store and is continuously inviting foodies from around the world for treatment. The way this fine dining restaurant has described the dishes as \"bringing the late French chef Paul Bocuse back to life\" has charmed its patrons."},{"type":"p","text":"Krasota, which offers an eight-course \"Imaginary Futures\" show, was co-founded by entrepreneur Boris Zarkov, renowned chef Vladimir Mukhin, and digital artist Anton Nenashev. Guests are taken through futuristic visions during this experience. Every course has a carefully chosen theme, which might be anything from space colonies to underwater cities, according to CNN."},{"type":"p","text":"Deepfake Technology and AI"},{"type":"p","text":"Krasota''s creative method is centered on its use of deepfake and AI technology to produce lifelike videos of the late, great chef Paul Bocuse, who passed away in 2018. In these videos, Bocuse talks about and explains the finer points of the food that is served. Deepfake algorithms and AI-generated projections are the technologies underlying this. The technologies are remarkably accurate in recreating the voice and likeness of Bocuse."},{"type":"p","text":"Nenashev used 3D computer graphics software to design the projections. On the other hand, Mukhin reinvented some of Bocuse''s most well-known dishes, like his truffle V.G.E soup, using the generative platform Midjourney. The end effect is a sense of the digital age that brings back memories and style of Bocuse. For the customers, dining here offers an alternative form of amusement and education."},{"type":"p","text":"Using Deepfake Videos Into The Dining"},{"type":"p","text":"The dining experience at Krasota incorporates the deepfake videos. A 20-seat circular table is surrounded by curved walls that act as projection screens in this dimly lit, round dining area. 3D video graphics are displayed on more than 20 projectors. These give life to the deepfake Bocuse. Then, with thorough explanations, the late chef leads the diners through each course."},{"type":"p","text":"This immersive setup is further enhanced by an artificial intelligence-powered interactive tabletop that has sensors to distinguish between different objects. Targeted projections, like fireflies on glasses and plates, are the result. In space-themed scenarios, there are interactive gaming elements as well, such as shooting passing spaceships."},{"type":"p","text":"According to Zarkov, there are several reasons to use deepfake and AI technology. Improving the dining experience''s educational and entertainment value is the main objective. Through the modernization of Bocuse''s culinary legacy, Krasota establishes a personal connection between the chef and the patrons. The restaurant honors his contributions to fine dining in this way."},{"type":"p","text":"In summary, Krasota is a shining example of culinary innovation in Dubai''s dynamic dining scene, where technology and the art of cooking coexist harmoniously. By leveraging artificial intelligence and deepfake technology, Krasota can bring diners into a multi-sensory experience that transports them to hypothetical futures while also bringing back the renowned Chef Paul Bocuse, who used his remarkable realism to explain and explain each dish. Krasota is a restaurant that was co-founded by industry pioneers Anton Nenashev, Vladimir Mukhin, and Boris Zarkov. It shows how artificial intelligence (AI) can go beyond traditional dining experiences by providing customers with more than just a meal; instead, it offers them an interactive exploration of culinary history and future possibilities."},{"type":"p","text":"By fusing state-of-the-art technology with exquisite culinary artistry, Krasota creates a lasting tribute to Chef Bocuse''s legacy while also providing entertainment and education. In addition to entertaining and educating guests, Krasota pays a heartfelt tribute to Chef Bocuse''s enduring legacy by Fusing state-of-the-art technology with exquisite culinary craftsmanship, imparting connections to the past with the most exquisite dining experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_c301d5990dc648c98428ddd39cc1242c~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_3000,h_2000,al_c,q_90/dubai.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-27', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('voice-ai-advancements:-soundhound-expands-restaurant-ordering', 'Voice AI Advancements: SoundHound Expands Restaurant Ordering', 'Transforming Dining Experiences with Advanced Voice AI Integration', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Transforming Dining Experiences with Advanced Voice AI Integration"},{"type":"p","text":"SoundHound AI announced Tuesday (June 18) the acquisition of key assets from Allset, an online food ordering platform, in another step toward further entrenching the voice artificial intelligence company within the restaurant industry."},{"type":"p","text":"SoundHound AI Acquires Allset Restaurant Network"},{"type":"p","text":"The transaction, the financial terms of which were not disclosed, brings almost 7,000 restaurant partners of Allset and engineering talent under the SoundHound umbrella. It also turns up the dial on further accelerating the development of voice ordering solutions for food service on cars, TVs, and other smart devices."},{"type":"p","text":"Advancing Voice AI in Food Service"},{"type":"p","text":"It''s an AI-powered speech technology-growing sector. As PYMNTS recently reported, McDonald''s ended its partnership with IBM to develop an AI-powered drive-thru system, deciding to pull the tech from more than 100 restaurants. A lot of what the fast-food chain has done underscores that challenges and opportunities are trailing behind the adoption of AI voice-ordering systems at a time when there is a general lack of labor and pressure on the industry for streamlined operations."},{"type":"p","text":"Voice AI is seen by SoundHound, which already works with over 10,000 restaurant locations, as a game-changing technology for the food service sector. Its systems allow for customer orders, support multiple languages, and are integrated directly with point-of-sale systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Challenges and Opportunities in AI-Powered Ordering"},{"type":"p","text":"Keyvan Mohajer, CEO and co-founder of SoundHound AI stated in the news release that \"combining forces, we will continue to deliver dynamic and convenient ways for people to order food items and complete a vast array of everyday transactions, just by talking naturally.\""},{"type":"p","text":"SoundHound''s Vision for Voice-Enabled Transactions"},{"type":"p","text":"The acquisition comes as restaurants get increasing recourse to technology to streamline operations and cut rising costs. The voice AI systems promise improved efficiency with automated order-taking and freeing of staff for other tasks."},{"type":"p","text":"Impact on Restaurant Operations and Costs"},{"type":"p","text":"Founded in 2015, Allset built its business around providing a platform for local food pickup that allowed restaurants and consumers to bypass exorbitant fees associated with delivery apps. The investment-backed company, with investors like Andreessen Horowitz, will bring its marketplace experience into SoundHound."},{"type":"p","text":"Allset''s Marketplace Expertise Joins SoundHound"},{"type":"p","text":"Stas Matviyenko, the co-founder and CEO of Allset, will bring his team to SoundHound. The news release said, \"We realized right away that we share the same vision for the voice commerce ecosystem that elevates the consumer experience.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Future Outlook: Voice Commerce in the Restaurant Industry"},{"type":"p","text":"Such integration of Allset''s restaurant relationships with the prowess of SoundHound voice AI could go on to fast-track mainstream adoption in voice ordering across a wide gamut of platforms. That ties well into the bigger picture, too, where tech giants and start-ups are racing to integrate voice assistants in a gamut of everyday consumer interactions."},{"type":"p","text":"With voice recognition technology improving day by day, voice commerce is expected to grow manifold in the next few years. SoundHound is increasing its investments in the Allset acquisition, this is one strategic move to help voice commerce grow with such a steep trend and be at the top among competitors in the Voice AI marketplace."},{"type":"p","text":"The acquisition of key assets from Allset by SoundHound AI becomes a gigantic step to enhance its capabilities in voice artificial intelligence in restaurants. This strategic acquisition brings almost 7,000 restaurant partners and engineering talent, further benefiting SoundHound on its commitment to changing food service through innovative technology."},{"type":"p","text":"Through this integration, Allset''s marketplace experience will combine with SoundHound''s leading-edge voice AI technology to bring much-needed dynamic enhancements across multiple platforms in customer interaction and operational efficiency. With industries turning toward automation and digital transformation, voice AI systems will help in easily taking orders and offsetting overload operationally during these constrained times of labor."},{"type":"p","text":"That development envisaged the broad challenges and potential of AI in restaurant operation optimization. With additional functionality, SoundHound can power such applications with natively seamless, multilingual voice interactions at the point of sale to drive further convenience and customer satisfaction."},{"type":"p","text":"Looking forward, given the potential rise of voice recognition technology, SoundHound wants to further grow voice commerce. With this acquisition, the company will be at the forefront of leading and prepared to play a major role in the transformation of consumer engagement with food service providers through smart, intuitive, and voice-controlled solutions."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_863093fb1b074d13a41f52a04040a2c0~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/102(27-june-news-blog-image).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-26', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('freedompay-and-toast-survey-reveals-key-focus:-data-security,-integration,-and-growth', 'FreedomPay and Toast Survey Reveals Key Focus: Data Security, Integration, and Growth', 'Enterprise Hospitality Insights: Data Security, Integration & Growth', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Enterprise Hospitality Insights: Data Security, Integration & Growth"},{"type":"p","text":"A recent study by FreedomPay, the global leader in Next Level CommerceTM solutions aligned with Toast, the leading cloud-based restaurant management software company, to bring important insights on what matters most to enterprise hospitality leaders. Key among these findings is the fact that data security, system integration, and enablement of growth are major critical vectors in the making of both merchant preference and trust within payment solutions and point-of-sale providers."},{"type":"p","text":"Key Takeaways from the Survey"},{"type":"p","text":"The survey gives crystal-clear insight into what enterprise hospitality leaders value most when selecting payment solutions and Point-of-sale systems. Notably, 53% of the overall population of merchants expressed a need for help in prioritizing their technology spend, which makes a strong business case for integrated solutions that can deliver full value and make informed decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"Data Security: An Issue of Paramount Importance"},{"type":"p","text":"The central finding that has emerged from the survey is that merchants unanimously agree on the issue of data security. All the participants believed that data security was important, although only 98% of them stated that data privacy is a major consideration in selecting a payment solution. In an era characterized by increased cyber threats, rigorous measures on security have never been needed more than now. Those providers that provide quality security protocols and adhere to standards, as validated by the PCI Security Standards Council in FreedomPay, will engender trust from a greater number of merchants."},{"type":"p","text":"Integration: The Basis of Operational Efficiency"},{"type":"p","text":"System integration as another critical factor comes out to be an area where most merchants would be looking to have a rather highly integrated system. The results of the survey suggest that 85% of merchants have their payment systems either fully integrated or integrated to a very high level with other software. Seamless integration means easy operations, accuracy of data, and a view of business performance in its entirety for informed decisions. This simplifies operations, reduces errors, and increases efficiency, generally making integrated solutions quite impossible to eliminate from modern hospitality businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"Customer Support and User Experience"},{"type":"p","text":"Good customer support was nominated by 49%, 46% said ease of use, and 44% said reliability. This shows that maybe the systems need to be reliable, accessible, and user-friendly. On the other hand, such responsive support services and easy interfaces considerably cut downtime and training costs, which increases productivity at large. It thus dawns on merchants that systems are important if they perform well but also need solid support behind them to ensure minimum disruption to operations."},{"type":"p","text":"Growth Enablement and Speed"},{"type":"p","text":"The attention to the enablement of growth, 82%, and operational speed, 81%, is indicative of the quest of merchants to meet the demands of the present and support future growth and flexibility. Scalability and flexibility of solutions can accommodate growth in business and dynamic market demands that offer strategic differentiation. Knowing customer behavior relative to shopping and purchasing patterns is core to enhancing customer experience and comprises the roadmap to sales."},{"type":"p","text":"Strategic Decision-Making"},{"type":"p","text":"The results of the survey point out that strategic decision-making concerning technology investments essentially boils down to a balancing act between innovation and mitigating risks. Hence, leaders are looking for integrated, secure, and efficient systems that can drive growth not at the cost of jeopardizing operations. Providers capable of delivering integrated, secure, and complete solutions may best fit such needs."},{"type":"p","text":"Industry Implications"},{"type":"p","text":"These insights draw attention to the areas of opportunities and the key focus areas for hospitality technology providers. From the strategic point of view, promotion of integration abilities, fortification of security measures, betterment of user experience, and strong customer support are some of the significant steps toward gaining and retaining enterprise clients. It is in aligning product development with these priorities that providers have the scope to satisfy dynamic industry requirements with some degree of effectiveness."},{"type":"p","text":"Conclusion"},{"type":"p","text":"The recent survey conducted by FreedomPay and Toast delivered important insight into security in data, integration, and enablement-driven growth at enterprise hospitality leaders. Providers of technologies should, therefore, focus on these key domains as a driver of solutions toward improved operational efficiency, increasing customer trust, and growing business. In this way, such technology providers will be aiding hospitality businesses to navigate the complexities of today''s commerce toward assured long-term success."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_5e694974229f47c5842dfe621bbb2773~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/103(27-june-blog-image).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-25', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('nyc-restaurant-owners-brace-for-potential-43%-delivery-app-fees', 'NYC Restaurant Owners Brace for Potential 43% Delivery App Fees', 'Will NYC Restaurants Survive a 43% Delivery Commission Hike? Owners Fear the Impact of Proposed Bill', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Will NYC Restaurants Survive a 43% Delivery Commission Hike? Owners Fear the Impact of Proposed Bill"},{"type":"p","text":"The New York City Council is currently reviewing a bill, Int 762, that could significantly alter the financial landscape for restaurants utilizing third-party delivery apps. The proposed legislation would allow apps like DoorDash, Uber Eats, and Grubhub to charge total commissions of up to 43% per order, a considerable increase from the current 23% cap."},{"type":"p","text":"Marketing Fees at the Center of Debate"},{"type":"p","text":"The most significant change under the proposed bill would impact marketing fees, potentially raising the current 5% cap to a maximum of 25%. This increase would allow restaurants to purchase additional visibility on the apps, potentially boosting their reach and competitiveness. However, this has sparked concerns about the financial burden on smaller businesses and the possibility of those unable to afford the higher fees being overshadowed."},{"type":"p","text":"Differing Perspectives on the Bill"},{"type":"p","text":"Delivery apps have voiced support for the bill, highlighting the potential benefits for restaurants in terms of flexibility and growth opportunities. However, restaurant advocates like the New York City Hospitality Alliance have raised concerns about the bill''s potential negative impact on small businesses. They argue that the increased fees could unfairly burden smaller establishments and create an uneven playing field."},{"type":"p","text":"New York City: A Unique Landscape for Delivery Fees"},{"type":"p","text":"New York City currently stands alone as the only city in the United States with permanent restrictions on delivery app fees. The proposed 43% ceiling in the bill even exceeds the typical charges in other markets, where a tiered model maxing out at 30% is the norm. This makes the bill a pivotal point in the ongoing debate over fair compensation and the impact of delivery apps on local businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"The Path Forward"},{"type":"p","text":"The bill, currently sponsored by 20 of the city''s 51 Council members, requires 26 votes to pass. As it progresses through the legislative process, the outcome of this debate will undoubtedly shape the future relationship between restaurants and delivery apps in New York City."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_72a7191c9a264481bb9f582801f8fac5~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/98-(25-new-blog)%20(1).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-24', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('pbna-strengthens-western-u.s.-presence-with-new-colorado-distribution-facility', 'PBNA Strengthens Western U.S. Presence with New Colorado Distribution Facility', 'PBNA Expands Footprint with State-of-the-Art Distribution Hub in Colorado, USA', '[{"type":"h2","text":"PBNA Expands Footprint with State-of-the-Art Distribution Hub in Colorado, USA"},{"type":"p","text":"PepsiCo Beverages North America (PBNA) recently unveiled a new 115,000-square-foot distribution center in Colorado Springs, significantly enhancing its distribution network and inventory capacity. This state-of-the-art facility allows PBNA to quadruple its previous capacity, ensuring efficient delivery of popular brands like Pepsi, Gatorade, Celsius, and Rockstar to consumers across Colorado and the broader US market."},{"type":"p","text":"Sustainable Design and Technology at the Forefront"},{"type":"p","text":"The Colorado Springs facility is a testament to PepsiCo''s commitment to sustainability. Equipped with solar panels to power delivery fleet pallet jacks, the facility is designed with a roof that can accommodate future solar expansion, reducing reliance on traditional energy sources. The implementation of LED motion-controlled lighting and an EV conduit installation further underscore the company''s dedication to minimizing its environmental impact."},{"type":"p","text":"Global Investments Strengthen PepsiCo''s Position"},{"type":"p","text":"This new facility is just one part of PepsiCo''s broader strategy to invest in its global infrastructure and enhance its distribution network. The company recently announced a $160 million investment in a new salty snacks plant in Kazakhstan, expanding its international presence. Additionally, PepsiCo invested £8 million in its Pipers Crisps manufacturing site in the UK and NR 12.66 billion (approx. $151.7 million) in a new flavor manufacturing facility in India, solidifying its position as a global leader in the food and beverage industry."},{"type":"p","text":"Commitment to Innovation and Sustainability"},{"type":"p","text":"By continually investing in cutting-edge facilities and sustainable technologies, PepsiCo demonstrates its commitment to innovation, efficiency, and responsible business practices. The Colorado Springs expansion exemplifies the company''s dedication to meeting growing consumer demand while minimizing its environmental footprint. This strategic move sets a new industry standard, showcasing PepsiCo''s leadership in both operational excellence and environmental stewardship."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_06464bcbf5cf439ba3f4e85586e68d4b~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/image%20(20).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-22', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('new-york-bill-outlaws-black-market-for-restaurant-reservations', 'New York Bill Outlaws Black Market for Restaurant Reservations', 'NY Cracks Down on Reservation Resellers', '[{"type":"h2","text":"NY Cracks Down on Reservation Resellers"},{"type":"p","text":"In June, a bill was passed in New York that forbade the sale of reservations obtained via automated systems on Internet forums. We are awaiting the signature of Governor Kathy Hochul on the Restaurant Reservation Anti-Piracy Act."},{"type":"p","text":"Defying Predatory Software"},{"type":"p","text":"According to a press release, if she signs it, New York will spearhead national efforts to combat the \"trend of predatory software flooding the online restaurant reservation marketplace.\" Given that it already has what are arguably the most fierce reservation wars in the country, New York is well-positioned to be the first."},{"type":"p","text":"The Struggle for Prime Reservations"},{"type":"p","text":"Are you trying to get three people into Carbone on a Friday night at six o''clock? Never even bother. The emergence of reservation platforms in New York, such as Resy, Opentable, Tock, and SevenRooms, has turned the competition for available slots into a reality show. People naturally devised methods to game systems. In these forums, a lot of reservations are made by bots, so it was never really a war to wait until midnight for a restaurant to open for business for the month."},{"type":"p","text":"Creating a Culture of Exclusivity"},{"type":"p","text":"The bill''s supporters claim that it has created a culture in which the wealthy and destitute must pay hundreds of dollars simply to obtain a reservation, and that''s before the expensive meal bills at restaurants."},{"type":"p","text":"Eater revealed in 2022 that finance bros created a closed online group chat on the encrypted messaging app Telegram called #FreeRezy, which included members of the Chainsmokers band as users. #FreeRezy was eventually discovered, but other groups have since taken its place. At the time, #FreeRezy told Eater, \"The benefit to someone in the group is you don''t have to plan a month.\""},{"type":"p","text":"\"People in their twenties lead hectic lives.\" Restaurants have also been left in the dark by untrustworthy reservations and a wave of cancellations from untrustworthy patrons. Many restaurants now charge no-show fees in its place."},{"type":"p","text":"Legitimate Reasons for the Black Market"},{"type":"p","text":"The black market may have grown for a few acceptable reasons: Following a positive COVID test, users on the Reddit group R/FoodNYC tried to hawk their nonrefundable, $1500 fine dining reservations during the omicron wave. The subReddit has continued to be used as a platform for reservation transfers in the years that have passed."},{"type":"p","text":"R/FoodNYC is primarily about discussions about food in New York, such as what to eat after the theater, so this was not its intended use. Eater receives a warning from a group moderator that anyone who upcharges on their non-refundable reservation trades risks being removed from the group."},{"type":"p","text":"Legislative Support and Industry Backing"},{"type":"p","text":"Applauded by the New York State Restaurant Association is bill S.9365/A.10215. \"New Yorkers should not have to pay shady middlemen just for the right to a dinner reservation,\" Assemblymember Alex Bores backed it as well. We are making sure that families won''t have to pay a $250, $500, or even $1,000 cover charge to celebrate a graduation, anniversary, or birthday thanks to this legislation."},{"type":"p","text":"We also shield workers from missing tips and restaurants from an increase in cancellations. genuinely win-win-win OpenTable and Resy are joining the chorus of supporters, which makes sense because it increases the relevance of their respective platforms in particular. The bill is \"a significant step forward to protect restaurants and diners from reservation fraud,\" according to Pablo Rivero, CEO of Resy."},{"type":"p","text":"Looking Ahead"},{"type":"p","text":"If enacted, this legislation may serve as a template for other states facing comparable challenges. It is a big step toward guaranteeing equitable access to reservations for dining and shielding customers and the restaurant business from dishonest business practices. A testament to New York''s dedication to preserving the integrity of its thriving dining scene is the Restaurant Reservation Anti-Piracy Act."},{"type":"p","text":"As evidence of its dedication to maintaining justice and openness in the restaurant business, New York has established a precedent in the fight against reservation fraud. In addition to safeguarding customers, this law creates a more reliable and long-lasting atmosphere that is conducive to restaurant success. This legislation could have a nationwide effect, changing reservation procedures and ensuring that everyone has a safe and enjoyable dining experience as other states take notice and may even implement comparable legislation."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_b42b9e1136644d67af32baa470843626~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/blxk%20marejt.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-21', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('ready,-set,-nominate!-2024-automation-&-self-service-awards-are-calling', 'Ready, Set, Nominate! 2024 Automation & Self-Service Awards are Calling', 'Deadline Approaching: Submit Your Groundbreaking Solutions Today!', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Deadline Approaching: Submit Your Groundbreaking Solutions Today!"},{"type":"p","text":"Hey there, tech trailblazers and automation aficionados! The time has come to put a spotlight on the game-changers who are revolutionizing how we interact with technology and services. Nominations for the 2024 Automation & Self-Service Awards are in full swing, and it''s an event you won''t want to miss."},{"type":"p","text":"Why These Awards Matter"},{"type":"p","text":"Picture this: a world where your daily tasks are streamlined, your customer experiences are seamless, and your business operations are humming with efficiency. That''s the future that automation and self-service are building, and these awards celebrate the companies and individuals at the forefront of that movement."},{"type":"p","text":"These aren''t your average awards - they''re a recognition of ingenuity, a platform for knowledge sharing, and a celebration of the endless possibilities that technology holds. By participating, you''re not just vying for a shiny trophy; you''re joining a community of innovators who are shaping the way we live and work."},{"type":"p","text":"Your Ticket to Recognition and Inspiration"},{"type":"p","text":"Whether you''re a nimble startup or an industry titan, these awards are designed to showcase your accomplishments. Imagine the buzz generated when your groundbreaking solution takes center stage, attracting the attention of potential customers, investors, and partners."},{"type":"p","text":"Beyond the prestige, the awards ceremony at the Self-Service Innovation Summit in Tampa is a prime opportunity for networking. Rub shoulders with industry leaders, exchange ideas with fellow innovators, and gain insights that can propel your business to new heights."},{"type":"p","text":"But it''s not all about the glitz and glamour. The Automation & Self-Service Awards are also a source of inspiration. By showcasing real-world applications of automation and self-service, we can spark new ideas, ignite conversations, and encourage even greater innovation across industries."},{"type":"p","text":"The Path to Nomination: Easy as 1, 2, 3"},{"type":"p","text":"1. Check Your Calendar: Ensure your project was completed after October 1, 2023."},{"type":"p","text":"2. Choose Your Categories: Decide which of the six categories best align with your innovation (you can enter multiple categories)."},{"type":"p","text":"3. Submit by September 6th: Complete the nomination form with a $200 fee per category (except for the \"Influencer of the Year\" category, which is free)."},{"type":"p","text":"The Categories: Where Your Innovation Shines"},{"type":"ul","items":["Best Vending Solution: Did you create a vending machine that''s more than just a snack dispenser? If it''s interactive, efficient, and user-friendly, this is your category.","Best Kiosk Solution: Have you designed a kiosk that elevates the customer experience, whether it''s for ordering, information access, or payments? This is where it belongs.","Best Use of Robotics: Are robots the stars of your show? If they''re performing tasks with precision and improving efficiency, this is their moment to shine.","Best Use of AI: Is artificial intelligence the brains behind your operation? If it''s powering smart interactions, data analysis, or customer service, let''s see it in action.","Responsible Innovation Award: Does your solution not only solve problems but also address social responsibility concerns like sustainability, accessibility, and inclusivity? This award is for you.","Influencer of the Year: Know someone who''s a driving force in the automation and self-service space? Nominate this trailblazer (for free!) and give them the recognition they deserve."]},{"type":"p","text":"The Countdown Begins"},{"type":"p","text":"The clock is ticking, innovators! Don''t miss your chance to be part of this celebration of ingenuity and progress. Click here today and share your story with the world. We can''t wait to see the incredible ways you''re shaping the future of automation and self-service."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_eb235d3c2d25421a8d35c54815aadc7c~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/Industry%20News%20June%2020.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-20', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('melt-bar-&-grilled,-gourmet-grilled-cheese-chain,-files-for-bankruptcy', 'Melt Bar & Grilled, Gourmet Grilled Cheese Chain, Files for Bankruptcy', 'Financial struggles force closure of multiple locations in recent years.', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Financial struggles force closure of multiple locations in recent years."},{"type":"p","text":"Melt Bar & Grilled, the renowned Cleveland-based restaurant chain celebrated for its gourmet grilled cheese sandwiches and vast craft beer selection, has officially filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection. The company attributes this decision to the escalating cost of goods and labor, which have significantly impacted its financial stability."},{"type":"p","text":"From Expansion to Downsizing"},{"type":"p","text":"Established in 2006 by Matt Fish, Melt Bar & Grilled experienced rapid growth, reaching over a dozen locations by 2017. However, the company has since faced economic headwinds, leading to the closure of multiple outlets. Currently, Melt Bar & Grilled operates four restaurants in Ohio, located in Akron, Lakewood, Mentor, and Columbus."},{"type":"p","text":"Financial Challenges and Liabilities"},{"type":"p","text":"According to court documents, the company''s liabilities range from $1 million to $10 million, while its assets are estimated to be between $500,000 and $1 million. The bankruptcy filing reveals that Melt Bar & Grilled owes debts to over 100 creditors."},{"type":"p","text":"Restructuring for a Sustainable Future"},{"type":"p","text":"Melt Bar & Grilled aims to utilize the Chapter 11 bankruptcy process to restructure its operations and achieve long-term financial viability. The company believes that this strategic move will enable it to \"ensure its immediate survival and long-term future success.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Industry-Wide Bankruptcy Trend"},{"type":"p","text":"Melt Bar & Grilled''s bankruptcy filing is not an isolated incident. In recent years, numerous restaurant chains have faced similar challenges, leading to bankruptcy filings. Notable examples include Rubio''s, Red Lobster, Party Fowl, Boxer Ramen, Tijuana Flats, Sticky Fingers, Oberweis Dairy, and Foxtrot/Dom''s Kitchen."},{"type":"p","text":"Factors Contributing to Restaurant Bankruptcies"},{"type":"p","text":"Experts attribute the rise in restaurant bankruptcies to various factors, including:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Rising Inflation: The increasing cost of goods and labor has significantly squeezed profit margins for restaurants.","Supply Chain Disruptions: The COVID-19 pandemic and geopolitical events have caused supply chain disruptions, leading to shortages and price increases for essential ingredients and supplies.","Changing Consumer Preferences: Shifting consumer preferences towards healthier and more diverse dining options have posed challenges for some traditional restaurant concepts."]},{"type":"p","text":"Future Outlook"},{"type":"p","text":"As Melt Bar & Grilled navigates the bankruptcy process, the company''s future remains uncertain. Nation''s Restaurant News has reached out to the company for further comments on its restructuring plans and potential closures. The outcome of this bankruptcy filing will undoubtedly have significant implications for the restaurant industry as a whole."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_2a1b6d21afa24eff9f9abbb2dc6388f9~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/June%2019%20Industry%20News.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-19', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('industry-mourns-the-loss-of-culinary-visionary-james-kent', 'Industry Mourns the Loss of Culinary Visionary James Kent', 'A Tribute to Chef James Kent: Visionary, Innovator, Mentor', '[{"type":"h2","text":"A Tribute to Chef James Kent: Visionary, Innovator, Mentor"},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant fraternity is in deep mourning following the untimely passing of famous and hardworking, innovative, influential chef James Kent, who shaped the concept of fine dining on 15th June 2024. It is on the backdrop of this sad news that sent shockwaves in the community that many are recalling his great contributions and the irreparable void his absence will leave."},{"type":"p","text":"A Life Dedicated to Excellence in Culinary Arts"},{"type":"p","text":"James Kent, the co-owner and executive chef of Crown Shy and Saga in New York City, has been synonymous with good food and spontaneity for quite a while. Native New Yorker brought up in the city, it didn''t take him very long before getting interested in food. He pursued his dreams vigorously, enrolling at the Prestigious Culinary Institute of America, where he began coming into his own as amazingly talented food-wise. Kent''s rise in the profession was not something less than extraordinary, a former employee of Jean-Georges and Eleven Madison Park, those highly celebrated establishments in which, in early days of work in the profession, he polished his craft and learned esteem for his unique culinary voice."},{"type":"p","text":"Crown Shy and Saga: Hallmarks of Innovation"},{"type":"p","text":"It wasn''t until 2019, with the opening of Crown Shy, that his vision began to take form. The new venture was soon critically acclaimed for its many creative dishes and great dining experience. Nestled in the Financial District, Crown Shy became a vantage point for modern American cuisine, what Kent calls marrying simplicity with sophistication. Crown Shy has established itself as a hot destination not just for everyday diners but for food lovers, too, within a respectably short period."},{"type":"p","text":"After Crown Shy''s success, in 2022 Kent opened Saga with his business partner, Jeff Katz. Located in a historic Art Deco building, Saga proved to be the real clincher on Kent''s résumé as a culinary provocateur. Tasting menus at the restaurant paid homage to Kent''s travels around the world and the diverse food scene of New York. All of these places have huge critical acclaim, with accolades from the Michelin Guide, and are now deeply entrenched as a part of New York dining."},{"type":"p","text":"Remembering a Culinary Giant"},{"type":"p","text":"Kent''s sudden death at 45 has been profound both personally and professionally for all the people who knew him. Many colleagues and friends, and several patrons, went online or used other means to express condolence messages and share their memories of the chef. \"James was not just a chef; he was a mentor, a friend, and a visionary. He will be incredibly missed,\" Katz said in a moving statement. Indeed, many have used this very comment, which speaks to Kent''s generosity, warmth, and inspiration to so many young chefs."},{"type":"p","text":"Celebrity chefs and culinary luminaries have joined in the tribute. \"James had a very special gift for making each person he encountered feel embraced and motivated. His love for cooking was contagious, and the ease with which his imagination flowed was incomparable,\" praised Daniel Humm of Eleven Madison Park."},{"type":"p","text":"The Industry Reflects and Presses On"},{"type":"p","text":"The tragic loss of Kent sends shockwaves throughout the restaurant world, renewing calls for mental health and support for it. The pressure-cooker environment of the culinary world, endless hours at work, constant scrutiny, starts to chip away, even at the toughest of emotions. Industry leaders call for more resources and support systems."},{"type":"p","text":"This is accompanied and balanced by the sudden surge of interest in doing even more in his memory: continuing to push the boundaries of culinary innovation and excellence. Of course, his restaurants Crown Shy and Saga naturally continue his vision and serve as living tributes to his extraordinary talent and dedication."},{"type":"p","text":"A Lasting Legacy"},{"type":"p","text":"The legacy of James Kent lives outside the realm of his restaurants; it is within young chefs whom he trained and in gastronomical dishes that are part of New York''s culinary tapestry. His way of cooking, where he blends tradition with modernity and simplicity with elegance, has forever left its mark on this industry."},{"type":"p","text":"The culinary community''s outpouring with that sense of grief and gratitude speaks to how strong of an impact he had on those around him. The contributions he made will remain part of the foundational makeup of the continuing story called American cuisine as the restaurant world progresses."},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant community gathers in celebration of James Kent''s life and all he has done, though it is amidst the sorrow and sense of loss that will never be the same again. His accomplishments, his love for food, his progressive nature, and his tenacious strive to personify the craft that he embodied shall never be forgotten and will always be a torch raised high for others who follow in his competitive culinary world. His passing is our collective loss, yet his legacy lives on in the further pursuit of the ideals of excellence and boundless imagination that he championed throughout these rich and storied years."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_43802270779e4b64913d712b9b8d5872~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/New%20blog.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-18', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('how-restaurants-are-financially-supporting-pride-month-initiatives?', 'How Restaurants Are Financially Supporting Pride Month Initiatives?', 'Restaurants Raising a Toast (and Funds) to the LGBTQ+ Community', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Restaurants Raising a Toast (and Funds) to the LGBTQ+ Community"},{"type":"p","text":"Pride month in June has become a big marketing opportunity for several brands and businesses including the restaurant industry. Gone are the days when rainbow logos were put on the menu or rainbow cupcakes were sold in limited quantities. Nowadays, restaurants are showing commitments to the LGBTQIA+ community beyond the vibrant aesthetics by supporting the displays of Pride month with real actions."},{"type":"p","text":"From Rainbow Washing to Purposeful Partnerships"},{"type":"p","text":"Earlier, many restaurants faced the backlash for “rainbow washing”. It is a term used to describe businesses that gain benefits from the Pride month symbols without providing enough support to the LGBTQIA+ community. But this year there is a change and we get to see more heartfelt gestures."},{"type":"p","text":"Following are a few examples of how the restaurants are using Pride Month marketing strategically."},{"type":"p","text":"Charity and Donation Partnerships"},{"type":"p","text":"Plenty of restaurants are collaborating with charities and LGBTQIA+ organizations. For instance: Chipotle Mexican Grill is sponsoring up to $25,000 towards GLAAD by selling their rainbow-themed merchandise, “The Pride Edit”. Customers at the register can also round up the amount of their orders with the proceeds going to GLAAD. Using this strategy, customers can have their favorite food and the amount they pay will be sent directly to a worthy cause."},{"type":"p","text":"Employee Empowerment and Inclusivity"},{"type":"p","text":"For LGBTQIA+ community restaurants are making changes by turning their work environment inclusive and friendly. Along with taking part in the Pride Parades, Mexican Chipotle is giving away five hundred “Love What Makes You Real” shirts to their staff members. All these acts show their dedication to fostering an atmosphere at work where diversity is respected."},{"type":"p","text":"Targeted Menu and Menu Promotions"},{"type":"p","text":"Although we may see limited-edition menu items, now they will serve a more significant function. For example, some restaurants might have a menu item curated especially for Pride Month with a donation to the charity for LGBTQIA+ charity."},{"type":"p","text":"The Gen Z Influence and The Rise of Consumer Activism"},{"type":"p","text":"There are plenty of reasons why the marketing for Pride Month has changed and become something more intentional. Firstly, people are becoming more conscious of the growing practice of “rainbow washing” and hold brands responsible for their actions. A big part of this is social media as it has the power to magnify voices and initiate conversations. Gen Z has also become a significant force in the movement. They are the generation known for their support of LGBTQIA+ rights and social activism. Due to this demographic influence, restaurants are adjusting their strategies for marketing."},{"type":"p","text":"Beyond the Rainbow: Addressing Long-Term Issues"},{"type":"p","text":"Although it is a good start to see purposeful marketing strategies during the Pride month, it is critical to recognize that genuine inclusivity extends beyond these short-term campaigns. Earlier there have been problems with the inclusion of LGBTQIA+ and representation in the workforce of restaurants. Restaurants can choose to aim for long-term growth in the following areas:"},{"type":"p","text":"Accessible Restrooms"},{"type":"p","text":"An important step towards the direction of inclusivity would be providing gender-neutral restrooms. This change will show their dedication to meet the needs of every customer, regardless of their gender identity."},{"type":"p","text":"Workplace Diversity and Training"},{"type":"p","text":"It is a constant work for restaurants and other businesses to create an environment at work that is entirely inclusive. These businesses should ensure a welcoming environment for their employees, despite their gender identity or sexual orientation, by inclusive training and investing in the diversity of their staff."},{"type":"p","text":"The Future of Restaurant Marketing During Pride Month"},{"type":"p","text":"It is a good idea for restaurants to provide emphasis on purpose-driven marketing in the Pride Month. It shows a change away from the grand gestures and makes the dining experience more inclusive for each person. Restaurants that give priority to employee empowerment, meaningful partnerships, and inclusivity for the long term are the ones that truly resonate with the customers and foster loyalty. This is because customers demand authenticity and social responsibility from brands. Following are a few trends for the future."},{"type":"p","text":"Hyper-Personalization"},{"type":"p","text":"With Pride Month offerings and promotions, restaurants should use customer insights and data to target particular customer segments of the LGBTQIA+ community."},{"type":"p","text":"Cause-Related Marketing Partnerships"},{"type":"p","text":"Having long-term collaborations between LGBTQIA+ and eateries may result in co-branded menu items, projects, and activities that have a significant impact."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants can turn marketing in Pride Month from a passing pad into a meaningful way to show support to the LGBTQIA+ community by placing a high value on inclusivity and embracing purpose. Thus, it will strengthen the bonds with customers, boost customer loyalty, and eventually propel long-term success."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_22036d151b3e4d12aa8ec55a057f857c~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/89-(14-june-news-blog-image2).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-17', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('the-oscars-of-the-food-world:-2024-james-beard-awards', 'The Oscars of the Food World: 2024 James Beard Awards', 'The Oscars of the Food World: 2024 James Beard Awards Highlight AI in Restaurants', '[{"type":"h2","text":"The Oscars of the Food World: 2024 James Beard Awards Highlight AI in Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"The 2024 James Beard Foundation Awards, often referred to as the \"Oscars of the food world,\" celebrated culinary brilliance while shining a spotlight on diverse American regions and cultures that are sometimes overlooked."},{"type":"p","text":"Celebrating Culinary Diversity"},{"type":"p","text":"Chef Serigne Mbaye''s Dakar NOLA, the winner of Best New Restaurant, garnered attention for its modern Senegalese tasting menu, which artfully blends ingredients from New Orleans with Mbaye''s West African heritage. The awards ceremony, held at the Lyric Opera of Chicago, provided a platform for Mbaye to express his pride in showcasing West African cuisine."},{"type":"p","text":"The James Beard Foundation Awards highlighted culinary talent from various backgrounds and regions, featuring winners who presented cuisines from the Philippines, Mexico, Japan, Peru, Vietnam, and Senegal, among others. This year''s awards recognized establishments in smaller cities and states that had not previously received James Beard Awards, signifying a broader recognition of culinary excellence across the country."},{"type":"p","text":"Honoring Smaller Towns and States"},{"type":"p","text":"Chef Paul Smith of 1010 Bridge in Charleston, West Virginia, made history as the first winner from West Virginia, receiving the Best Chef: Southeast award. Lula Drake Wine Parlour in Columbia, South Carolina, was honored with the Best Wine and Other Beverage Program award. The awards also acknowledged chefs from Easton, Maryland; Mystic, Connecticut; and Mission, Texas, further emphasizing the diversity of culinary talent across the United States."},{"type":"p","text":"New Culinary Careers"},{"type":"p","text":"The James Beard Awards celebrated chefs who found their culinary calling through unique journeys. Masako Morishita, originally from Japan, transitioned from cheering for the Washington Commanders to winning the Emerging Chef Award for her Japanese comfort food at Perry''s in Washington, DC. Atsuko Fujimoto, who moved to Portland, Maine, 23 years ago without any prior professional kitchen experience, was honored with the Outstanding Baker award."},{"type":"p","text":"Addressing Industry Challenges"},{"type":"p","text":"The event addressed critical issues facing the restaurant industry, including mental health, inclusivity, climate change, and sustainability. Ruth Reichl, a renowned food writer who received a Lifetime Achievement Award, acknowledged the James Beard Foundation''s role in transforming American cuisine. She had coined the phrase \"Oscars of the food world\" over three decades ago in her reporting on the inaugural awards."},{"type":"p","text":"The James Beard Foundation, a non-profit organization founded in 1986, has implemented new rules and guidelines to address past criticisms regarding lack of diversity and misconduct by chefs. Winners expressed optimism that positive changes in culinary culture will continue, with Best Chef: Northwest & Pacific winner Gregory Gourdet emphasizing the importance of female-led teams, diversity, and inclusivity."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurant and Chef Award Winners"},{"type":"ul","items":["Outstanding Chef: Michael Rafidi, Albi, Washington, D.C.","Outstanding Restaurant: Kann, Portland, Oregon","Best New Restaurant: The Restaurant at Justin, Justin, Texas","Emerging Chef: Rene Redzepi, Noma, Copenhagen, Denmark & Brooklyn, New York","Outstanding Bar: Julep, Houston","Outstanding Pastry Chef or Baker: Margarita Manzke, République, Los Angeles","Outstanding Hospitality: Sepia, Chicago"]},{"type":"p","text":"Best Chefs by Region"},{"type":"ul","items":["California: Brandon Jew, Mister Jiu''s, San Francisco","Great Lakes: Andrew Zimmerman and Mike Delay, Sepia, Chicago","Mid-Atlantic: Peter Chang, Peter Chang, multiple locations","Midwest: Yia Vang, Union Hmong Kitchen, Minneapolis","Mountain: Caroline Glover, Annette, Aurora, Colorado","New York State: Chintan Pandya, Dhamaka, New York City","Northeast (excluding New York State): Valentine Howell, The Beehive, Bristol, Rhode Island","Northwest & Pacific: Crystal Wahpepah, Wahpepah''s Kitchen, Oakland, California","South: Terry Koval, The Deer and the Dove, Decatur, Georgia","Southeast: Mashama Bailey, The Grey, Savannah, Georgia","Southwest: Fernando Olea, Sazón, Santa Fe, New Mexico","Texas: Iliana de la Vega, El Naranjo, Austin"]},{"type":"p","text":"Note: The list of winners above is not exhaustive. For a complete list of winners and nominees, please refer to the official James Beard Foundation website."},{"type":"p","text":"The 2024 James Beard Foundation Awards showcased a vibrant and evolving culinary landscape in the United States, celebrating diversity, regional flavors, and the dedication of chefs and restaurateurs to their craft. The awards also acknowledged the challenges faced by the industry while emphasizing the importance of inclusivity and sustainability."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_4f0bfce3a02342aba02b85b8127e6940~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/93(17june-News-blog).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-16', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('franchise-fever:-2024-expo-ignites-entrepreneurial-spirit-with-thousands-of-attendees', 'Franchise Fever: 2024 Expo Ignites Entrepreneurial Spirit with Thousands of Attendees', 'Thousands Flock to 2024 Franchise Expo, Fueling Business Ambitions', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Thousands Flock to 2024 Franchise Expo, Fueling Business Ambitions"},{"type":"p","text":"The 2024 International Franchise Expo (IFE) enjoyed gorgeous weather in New York City last week, welcoming thousands of attendees to the iconic Javits Center. Over 300 franchise exhibitors showcased a diverse range of industries, from automotive and beauty to technology and food. Attendees were eager to discover new brands, network with industry professionals, and learn from educational sessions."},{"type":"p","text":"Innovative Concepts Take Center Stage"},{"type":"p","text":"On the show floor, the On the Hook food truck concept stood out. President Ocean Andrew, son of an Alaskan fisherman, emphasized the brand''s focus on family-friendly work hours and community-based operations. Colette Bell, founder of Ace Handyman, highlighted the importance of customer service in driving their success as the top handyman franchise in the country."},{"type":"p","text":"Franchise Vendors and Suppliers Offer Key Support"},{"type":"p","text":"The expo also featured numerous vendors and suppliers crucial to franchise success. Sebastian Aguirre of NiceJob shared how his company has helped hundreds of franchises with online reputation management. The franchise law firm Spadea Lignana showcased their cloud-based system for simplifying Franchise Disclosure Document updates."},{"type":"p","text":"Educational Sessions Empower Aspiring Franchisees"},{"type":"p","text":"IFE 2024 offered over 70 workshops and sessions. The \"Women in Franchising: Being Successful in Today’s Marketplace\" panel featured accomplished women sharing insights on teamwork, mentorship, and the importance of diversity in business. Steve Beagelman of SMB Franchise Advisors presented \"Should You Franchise Your Business?\", guiding potential franchisors through key considerations like control, communication, and capital requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"Culinary Delights and Industry Trends"},{"type":"p","text":"Attendees enjoyed a plethora of food samples, with chicken being a dominant theme among exhibitors. Beyond specific franchises, the expo highlighted trends like sustainability, technology integration in services, and the growing wellness industry."},{"type":"p","text":"Networking and Collaboration Opportunities Abound"},{"type":"p","text":"IFE served as a vital hub for networking and collaboration. Attendees connected with fellow entrepreneurs, industry experts, and franchisors, fostering potential partnerships and investments."},{"type":"p","text":"The Future of Franchising"},{"type":"p","text":"The trends showcased at IFE 2024 point to a bright future for the franchising sector. Businesses are embracing technology to meet evolving consumer demands, with a growing emphasis on sustainability and innovation. The expo''s success underscores the resilience and adaptability of the franchise model, promising continued growth and evolution in the years to come."},{"type":"p","text":"Overall, the 2024 International Franchise Expo provided a comprehensive look at the current landscape and future potential of the franchising industry, leaving attendees inspired and eager for the next edition."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_1407826a91cd45c3951e2e5710ff6148~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/80-(13june-News-report).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-15', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('mcdonald’s-empowers-black-fashion-designers-with-new-initiative', 'McDonald’s Empowers Black Fashion Designers with New Initiative', 'Beyond the Golden Arches: McDonald''s New Program Elevates Black Fashion Talent', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Beyond the Golden Arches: McDonald''s New Program Elevates Black Fashion Talent"},{"type":"p","text":"To encourage and assist Black fashion designers, McDonald''s launches the Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion initiative. Due to the low percentage of Black designers in the United States (7.3%), the McDonald''s program is extremely important. McDonald''s I addressed the issues of diversity in the industry with this launch. Given that this program is a comprehensive undertaking, its launch has had a significant impact on interest. For a year-long mentorship, this initiative pairs five up-and-coming designers with five seasoned Black industry professionals."},{"type":"p","text":"This handbook contains industry insights, useful suggestions, and the mentors'' individualized coaching. These revelations would impede the designer''s career advancement. The launch of a capsule collection that showcases the undeniable and extraordinary talent of the chosen designers."},{"type":"p","text":"Financial and Mentorship Support:"},{"type":"p","text":"The biggest problem that black designers have is funding, which McDonald''s addresses. The designers don''t have to worry about the money for creating the designs, they can concentrate on creating the designs with no tension as McDonald''s provided a total of $200,000 in financial funding. The master classes that are conducted by experienced designers provide them the insight into the industry guidelines and serve as a helping hand. This knowledge would help the designers in the long run."},{"type":"p","text":"Impact and Importance:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion initiative from McDonald''s encourages diversity and the advancement of Black designers in the fashion sector. The goal of this initiative is to empower black designers to spur change within the industry. McDonald''s is prepared to keep highlighting the accomplishments and potential of Black designers, as it has done well in the past. The well-known mentors would help the designers succeed and provide them with insightful advice. Famous designers Elaine Welteroth and Jacqueline Cooper have been brought in by McDonald''s to coach the designers and provide them with vital industry insights and guidance."},{"type":"p","text":"Broader Campaign Context:"},{"type":"p","text":"The empowerment of the Black community is the main goal of McDonald''s large Black and Positively Golden initiative. McDonald''s has already taken several actions in this regard and is still doing well. It started back in 2019 to offer a successful helping hand. This initiative has helped the black community and brought an empowering change. McDonald''s has ensured to help in various spheres including education and empowerment. The Change of Fashion program, which highlights the brand''s long-term dedication to supporting the Black community, is the campaign''s extension."},{"type":"p","text":"Personal Stories:"},{"type":"p","text":"The show includes personal stories, Larissa Muehleder''s being one of them. Larissa''s story serves as an excellent example of how the program can significantly impact Black designers'' careers. It disproves the designers'' positive experiences and the way it changed their lives."},{"type":"p","text":"Future Implications:"},{"type":"p","text":"The success of McDonald''s Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion initiative serves as a model for other businesses. It inspires people to support Black creators with comparable endeavors. There has been a long-lasting positive influence from these programs. McDonald''s has demonstrated an extraordinary commitment to social responsibility, and these activities are valued by the company''s devoted consumer base."},{"type":"p","text":"Expanding Opportunities:"},{"type":"p","text":"Opportunities under the McDonald''s Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion program have increased. This initiative benefits individual designers as well as providing opportunities inside the fashion industry. This curriculum encourages a diversified worldview and questions accepted industry conventions. Through this program, a more positive perspective has been brought to the globe by displaying the brilliance and originality of Black designers."},{"type":"p","text":"Through cooperation and mentoring, aspiring designers could get access to networks and resources that were previously unavailable. They have achieved long-term success as a result. The fashion business now offers more chances and is more representative of a range of views and experiences thanks to this program."},{"type":"p","text":"McDonald’s Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion program is a commendable move in the direction of expansion and diversity. It has addressed the critical void present in the fashion sector. McDonald''s has given Black designers media visibility, financial backing, and mentoring. This not only advances the careers of these designers but also brings about a shift in the industry as a whole. This initiative is a calculated part of McDonald''s continuous attempts to promote inclusivity and diversity, enhancing the company''s reputation as a socially conscious one."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_0e321335e614411792096823f2c39a1f~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/image%20(14).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-14', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('experience-l.a.''s-unique-pizza-fusion:-cheesy-crusts-and-korean-bbq-toppings', 'Experience L.A.''s Unique Pizza Fusion: Cheesy Crusts and Korean BBQ Toppings', 'Korean BBQ Pizza: L.A.''s Unexpected & Delicious Food Fusion Trend', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Korean BBQ Pizza: L.A.''s Unexpected & Delicious Food Fusion Trend"},{"type":"p","text":"Los Angeles is renowned for its multiculturalism, which extends to the sense of taste. L.A.''s unique pizza culture is renowned for its flavor fusions. There are currently a tonne of alternatives due to the innovation in pizza culture, which started with traditional experiments and moved into modern ones. From the first, innovative smoked salmon pizza to the newest craze of Korean BBQ toppings. The evolution of L.A.''s pizza culture is evidence of the city''s spirit of culinary innovation."},{"type":"p","text":"The unmatched pizza experience of L.A. is all about the classical taste with international spice twists. Let''s take a tour around the colorful and varied world of pizza, emphasizing the places you simply must see and the creative tastes that characterize this thriving culinary scene."},{"type":"p","text":"The Birth of a Pizza Revolution"},{"type":"p","text":"When Wolfgang Puck introduced his smoked salmon pizza at Spago in the early 1980s, it revolutionized the pizza industry. This marked the start of Los Angeles'' transformation as a cosmopolitan center for pizza. His approach opened the door for other cooks to try new things. They brought in new tastes and aesthetics, resulting in a pizza culture that is constantly changing."},{"type":"p","text":"Embracing Diverse Styles"},{"type":"p","text":"The variety-rich L.A. pizza places are a landmark for the pizza lovers. Whether it be the cheesy crusts which are thick and chewy or the crispy foldable pizzas it covers so much and more. Each innovative pizza is better than the other inspired by the Neapolitan style. Every pizza enthusiast can find something to their liking. By incorporating regional ingredients and special techniques, the local chefs further enrich the diversity."},{"type":"p","text":"Fusion of Flavors: Korean BBQ Pizza"},{"type":"p","text":"Right now, combining the flavors of Korean BBQ with conventional pizza has to be one of the most interesting trends. This has given the pizza culture of Los Angeles a delicious touch. This combines the best elements of Korean and traditional flavors. Thus, the creative culture provides a distinctive experience that satisfies our palates."},{"type":"p","text":"Seven Tigers Pie Club"},{"type":"p","text":"We are introduced to the combination of Detroit-style pizza with L.A. and a dash of Korean ideas at this restaurant, which is headed by Alex Sign. This yields an incredibly delicious assortment of pizzas. These have fusion-type toppings that incorporate Korean BBQ ingredients into the classic Los Angeles style."},{"type":"p","text":"Notable Pizzerias Leading the Charge"},{"type":"p","text":"Many pizzerias in Los Angeles have expanded the definition of conventional pizza, resulting in distinctive and remarkable dining experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"One of the well-known is the Leopardo, which is run by chef Joshua Skenes, a renowned and highly acclaimed chef with an adventurous flair. Leopardo is about so much more than just homemade mozzarella. They leave no opportunities to impress with the wild-yeasted dough formed from stone ground floors. This eatery serves pizza created through experimentation and vivid combinations."},{"type":"p","text":"The Fiorelli Pizza, which comes from the Cooks Garden in Venice, is another item on the list. This one places more focus on using locally farmed and fresh ingredients. Their strategy promotes sustainability and guarantees high-quality products. Through its internet platform, it keeps a tight relationship with its clients."},{"type":"p","text":"Essential Pizzas to Try in L.A."},{"type":"p","text":"Pizza culture in Los Angeles is characterized by creativity, variety, and innovation. Let''s talk about some pizzas that highlight the culinary inventiveness of the city:"},{"type":"p","text":"First on the list is folk pizza, which is renowned for its tenacity in fermenting dough. This one has a wide, robust rim that preserves all of the components. To taste something different, try the traditional pepperoni or fennel sausage pizza."},{"type":"p","text":"The Pizzana, a contemporary twist on Neapolitan pizza, comes next. enhanced with discussions of locally grown veggies, other special sauces, and sausages produced in-house."},{"type":"p","text":"A must-try is the Gjelina. It was acclaimed for its wood-fired pizza which is fusions with tradition and modern-day innovation. Using toppings and seasonal, fresh foods."},{"type":"p","text":"These days, pizza enthusiasts flock to Los Angeles. It combines current innovation and diversity with traditional flavor. Whether you want to stick with traditional looks or take a bold step forward with cutting-edge fusions and experiments. Pizza culture in Los Angeles has something for everyone. Taste the fusion to give your taste buds an unparalleled experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_abbf08bfdde7414db2fcb560180ce78a~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_3000,h_2000,al_c/image%20(14).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-13', 'published');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO news_posts (slug, title, excerpt, body, cover_image, category, author_name, published_at, status) VALUES ('securing-the-plate:-the-restaurant-industry’s-cyber-fraud-battle', 'Securing the Plate: The Restaurant Industry’s Cyber Fraud Battle', 'Digital Dining Dangers: The Rising Threat of Cyberattacks on Restaurants', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Digital Dining Dangers: The Rising Threat of Cyberattacks on Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"In a time when technology is king, the fight against cybercrime has reached previously unprecedented heights. As the food industry is adjusting to the modern age, new measures are coming upfront to protect restaurant gift card transactions from online threats. To ensure that your meal is both safe and tasty, restaurants from all over the world are stepping up."},{"type":"p","text":"Embracing Digital Integration in Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"Any modern restaurant you visit is probably going to have a lot of digital gadgets that are all seamlessly incorporated into the dining experience. Our interactions with our favorite restaurants have been completely transformed by technology, from contactless payment methods to tablets for ordering. But these technological advances also bring vulnerabilities, so restaurateurs are strengthening their digital fortifications with every measure possible."},{"type":"p","text":"The Increasing Threat of Cyber Fraud"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Cyber Fraud is more common than ever, but there are a multitude of measures that can be implemented to ensure profits and customers don''t suffer,\" says Sivakumar Vinayagam, an expert in cybersecurity and software engineering. He is currently the Lead Systems Architect for Netmasons and its service Securetree, and he has over ten years of experience in the field."},{"type":"p","text":"Expertise in Restaurant Gift Card Security"},{"type":"p","text":"With almost 1,000 clients, Vinayagam is a software specialist in the restaurant gift card market. He works with different restaurant groups and, through his system implementations and programming skills, has saved businesses millions of dollars. \"I want small and medium-sized businesses to feel like they have security, substantial reach, and success even in the absence of substantial resources or time,\" he says."},{"type":"p","text":"Implementing Cutting-Edge Encryption"},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant industry''s primary line of defense against cyberattacks is encryption. According to Vinayagam, \"Restaurants thwart the attempts of cybercriminals aiming to intercept transactions by encoding sensitive information such as credit card details and customer data.\" To stop fraud, he uses distinct gift card numbers and keeps an eye out for odd activity."},{"type":"p","text":"Ensuring Robust Cybersecurity"},{"type":"p","text":"Vinayagam''s function as a cybersecurity expert depends heavily on these integrated security measures. It is possible to stop fraudsters from taking advantage of gift card systems by putting these safeguards in place, protecting both the consumers and the participating businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"Raising the Bar with PCI Compliance"},{"type":"p","text":"The standard for protecting credit card information is established by the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard or PCI DSS. Restaurants need to make sure that every part of their digital infrastructure satisfies the highest security standards by carefully following these strict guidelines. To guarantee compliance, Vinayagam places a strong emphasis on access control procedures and frequent network monitoring."},{"type":"p","text":"Heightened Vigilance Against Phishing Scams"},{"type":"p","text":"Phishing scams are still a major problem in the digital world, endangering both consumers and businesses. Restaurants are actively teaching their employees and customers how to spot phishing attempts. Vinayagam states, \"Eateries can stay one step ahead of cybercriminals by fostering a culture of vigilance.\" His proprietary Fraud Score system aids in identifying and examining questionable transactions."},{"type":"p","text":"Deploying Advanced Fraud Detection Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants are using sophisticated fraud detection systems as part of the ongoing arms race against cyber fraud. These systems analyze transactional data in real time to spot anomalies and questionable activity using machine learning and artificial intelligence algorithms. \"Eateries are protecting their customers and reputation by detecting fraudulent behavior before it escalates,\" claims Vinayagam."},{"type":"p","text":"Empowering Consumers with Security Awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"In the fight against cyber fraud, education is essential. Vinayagam states, \"Eateries need to educate consumers about the importance of secure transactions and the risks associated with cyber threats, whether through informative signage or digital campaigns.\" He thinks restaurants can increase customer loyalty and trust by cultivating a security-conscious culture."},{"type":"p","text":"Building Trust Through Security Consciousness"},{"type":"p","text":"According to Vinayagam, \"In an era where technology permeates every aspect of our lives, the fight against cyber fraud is more critical than ever.\" \"In my quest to protect against cyber threats, I worked hard to look into every possibility. I want both restaurant owners and patrons to feel secure and at ease.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Cybersecurity becomes essential as the restaurants embrace technology. PCI compliance, encryption, and fraud detection systems protect the gift card information. Educating diners and staff on cyber scams keeps everyone safe. By giving priority to security, restaurants can ensure a secure and delightful dining experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_f93c8d3dbb014f198ae95078d6af1ce0~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_4000,h_3000,al_c/cyber.png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-12', 'published');
